of his days drinking his food through a straw.</i>

679
00:45:54.938 --> 00:45:59.610
I'm thinking Andy could use a nice welcome
back when he gets out of the infirmary.

680
00:46:00.736 --> 00:46:04.531
Sounds good to us.
I figure we owe him that much for the beer.

681
00:46:05.908 --> 00:46:08.577
The man likes to play chess.

682
00:46:08.660 --> 00:46:10.746
Let's get him some rocks.

683
00:46:43.196 --> 00:46:45.073
Guys...

684
00:46:45.156 --> 00:46:47.534
I got one. I got one. Look.

685
00:46:49.953 --> 00:46:52.038
Heywood. that isn't soapstone.

686
00:46:52.121 --> 00:46:54.332
And it ain't alabaster. either.

687
00:46:54.415 --> 00:46:56.043
What are you. a fucking geologist?

688
00:46:56.126 --> 00:46:58.170
He's right. It ain't.

689
00:46:58.254 --> 00:46:59.505
Well. what the hell is it?

690
00:46:59.588 --> 00:47:02.132
RED: A horse apple.

691
00:47:02.216 --> 00:47:05.344
- Bullshit.
- No. horse shit. Petrified.

692
00:47:05.427 --> 00:47:07.513
(HORSE WHINNIES)

693
00:47:11.725 --> 00:47:14.603
- Oh. Jesus Christ!
(MEN LAUGH)

694
00:47:14.728 --> 00:47:16.647
Oh. damn!

695
00:47:16.772 --> 00:47:20.734
<i>RED: Despite a few hitches.
the boys came through in fine style.</i>

696
00:47:21.944 --> 00:47:24.572
<i>And by the weekend he was due back.
we had enough rocks</i>

697
00:47:24.655 --> 00:47:27.700
<i>to keep him busy till rapture.</i>

698
00:47:27.783 --> 00:47:30.494
<i>I also got a big shipment in that week.</i>

699
00:47:30.578 --> 00:47:33.122
<i>Cigarettes. Chewing gum.</i>

700
00:47:33.205 --> 00:47:34.708
<i>Sipping whisky.</i>

701
00:47:34.791 --> 00:47:38.336
<i>Playing cards with naked ladies on them.
You name it.</i>

702
00:47:38.420 --> 00:47:41.381
<i>And of course. the most important item.</i>

703
00:47:43.133 --> 00:47:45.218
<i>Rita Hayworth herself.</i>

704
00:48:19.420 --> 00:48:22.256
GUARD: OK. look alive! Open all tiers.

705
00:48:22.340 --> 00:48:24.675
(FURTIVELY) Heads up. They're tossing the cells.

706
00:48:24.759 --> 00:48:27.011
Heads up. They're tossing the cells.

707
00:48:29.138 --> 00:48:31.015
119.

708
00:48:32.516 --> 00:48:34.185
123.

709
00:48:34.769 --> 00:48:36.854
(GUARDS CALLING OUT)

710
00:48:44.153 --> 00:48:46.030
On your feet.

711
00:48:47.740 --> 00:48:49.618
Face the wall.

712
00:49:21.358 --> 00:49:23.443
HADLEY: Turn around and face the Warden.

713
00:49:29.659 --> 00:49:31.744
Pleased to see you reading this.

714
00:49:33.121 --> 00:49:35.414
Any favorite passages?

715
00:49:36.457 --> 00:49:41.587
"Watch ye. therefore. for ye know not
when the master of the house cometh."

716
00:49:42.630 --> 00:49:45.508
Mark 13:35.

717
00:49:45.591 --> 00:49:48.261
I always liked that one.

718
00:49:48.344 --> 00:49:49.846
But I prefer...

719
00:49:49.929 --> 00:49:52.682
"I'm the light of the world.

720
00:49:52.765 --> 00:49:56.310
He that followeth me shall not walk in darkness.
but shall have the light of life."

721
00:49:56.394 --> 00:49:58.980
John. Chapter 8. Verse 12.

722
00:49:59.063 --> 00:50:02.525
I hear you're good with numbers. How nice.

723
00:50:03.651 --> 00:50:05.737
A man should have a skill.

724
00:50:07.823 --> 00:50:09.283
Wanna explain this?

725
00:50:10.409 --> 00:50:13.871
It's called a rock blanket.
It's for shaping and polishing rocks.

726
00:50:14.913 --> 00:50:16.874
A little hobby of mine.

727
00:50:25.299 --> 00:50:27.634
(INHALES)

728
00:50:27.718 --> 00:50:30.721
It's pretty clean. Some contraband here.

729
00:50:30.804 --> 00:50:32.890
but nothing to get in a twist over.

730
00:50:36.727 --> 00:50:38.812
I can't say I approve of this.

731
00:50:40.314 --> 00:50:42.024
But I suppose...

732
00:50:43.985 --> 00:50:45.862
..exceptions can be made.

733
00:50:56.247 --> 00:50:58.541
HADLEY: Lock 'em up!

734
00:51:00.543 --> 00:51:02.503
I almost forgot.

735
00:51:02.587 --> 00:51:04.839
I'd hate to deprive you of this.

736
00:51:04.964 --> 00:51:06.424
Salvation lies within.

737
00:51:07.508 --> 00:51:08.843
Yes. sir.

738
00:51:17.143 --> 00:51:19.729
<i>RED: Tossing cells was just an excuse.</i>

739
00:51:20.272 --> 00:51:23.859
<i>The truth is. Norton wanted to size Andy up.</i>

740
00:51:37.498 --> 00:51:40.626
My wife made that in church group.

741
00:51:42.961 --> 00:51:44.296
Very nice. sir.

742
00:51:45.464 --> 00:51:47.341
Do you enjoy working in the laundry?

743
00:51:48.967 --> 00:51:50.677
No. sir. not especially.

744
00:51:50.761 --> 00:51:53.555
Perhaps we can find something more...

745
00:51:53.639 --> 00:51:55.724
befitting a man of your education.

746
00:52:00.063 --> 00:52:01.981
(BIRD SCREECHES)

747
00:52:04.109 --> 00:52:05.777
Hey. Jake. Where's Brooks?

748
00:52:05.860 --> 00:52:07.153
Andy.

749
00:52:07.237 --> 00:52:09.531
I thought I heard you out here!

750
00:52:11.032 --> 00:52:12.617
I've been reassigned to you.

751
00:52:12.700 --> 00:52:15.870
I know. They told me. (CHUCKLES)

752
00:52:15.954 --> 00:52:18.039
Ain't that a kick in the head?

753
00:52:18.123 --> 00:52:20.625
Well. I'll give you the dime tour.

754
00:52:20.708 --> 00:52:22.794
Come on.

755
00:52:22.877 --> 00:52:25.046
Well. here she is.

756
00:52:25.130 --> 00:52:27.674
Shawshank Prison library.

757
00:52:27.757 --> 00:52:30.635
National Geographics.

758
00:52:30.718 --> 00:52:33.555
Reader's Digest condensed books.

759
00:52:33.638 --> 00:52:35.933
Louis L'Amour.

760
00:52:35.933 --> 00:52:38.060
Look Magazine.

761
00:52:38.144 --> 00:52:40.646
Erle Stanley Gardners.

762
00:52:40.729 --> 00:52:44.275
Every evening.
I load up the cart and make my round.

763
00:52:44.275 --> 00:52:47.444
I enter the names on this clipboard here.

764
00:52:47.528 --> 00:52:50.990
Easy-peasy. Japanesey. Any questions?

765
00:52:51.073 --> 00:52:54.034
Brooks. how long have you been librarian?

766
00:52:54.160 --> 00:52:59.331
Oh...I come here in '05.
and they made me librarian in 1912.

767
00:52:59.415 --> 00:53:02.793
And in all that time.
have you ever had an assistant?

768
00:53:02.877 --> 00:53:05.462
No. No. not much to it. really.

769
00:53:05.546 --> 00:53:07.464
Well. why me? Why now?

770
00:53:07.548 --> 00:53:09.049
I don't know.

771
00:53:09.133 --> 00:53:12.469
but it'll be nice to have some company
down here for a change.

772
00:53:12.469 --> 00:53:14.556
HADLEY: Dufresne!

773
00:53:23.857 --> 00:53:25.942
That's him. That's the one.

774
00:53:33.491 --> 00:53:34.784
I'm Dekins.

775
00:53:34.868 --> 00:53:37.329
(NERVOUSLY) I was er...

776
00:53:37.412 --> 00:53:41.416
thinking about maybe setting up
some kind of trust fund for my kids' educations.

777
00:53:43.752 --> 00:53:45.211
Oh...

778
00:53:45.295 --> 00:53:46.963
I see.

779
00:53:48.423 --> 00:53:50.300
Well. erm...

780
00:53:51.677 --> 00:53:53.262
..why don't we have a seat.

781
00:53:53.346 --> 00:53:55.431
and talk it over?

782
00:53:57.975 --> 00:54:00.895
Brooks.
do you have a piece of paper and a pencil?

783
00:54:12.365 --> 00:54:14.075
Thanks.

784
00:54:14.158 --> 00:54:15.826
So...

785
00:54:17.078 --> 00:54:19.580
Mr. Dekins...

786
00:54:19.664 --> 00:54:24.126
And then Andy says to Mr. Dekins.
"Do you want your sons to go to Harvard.

787
00:54:24.210 --> 00:54:26.337
- or Yale?"
- He didn't say that?

788
00:54:26.420 --> 00:54:29.091
As God is my witness. he did!

789
00:54:29.174 --> 00:54:32.552
Dekins just blinked for a second.
Then he laughed himself silly.

790
00:54:32.636 --> 00:54:34.513
And afterwards he shook Andy's hand.

791
00:54:34.596 --> 00:54:35.972
My ass!

792
00:54:36.056 --> 00:54:37.265
Shook his hand.

793
00:54:37.349 --> 00:54:40.310
Hell. I...I near soiled myself! (LAUGHS)

794
00:54:40.394 --> 00:54:44.606
All Andy needed was a suit and a tie
and a little jiggly hula girl on his desk.

795
00:54:44.690 --> 00:54:46.024
AND HE WOULD HAVE BEEN:

796
00:54:46.149 --> 00:54:47.693
"Mr. Dufresne. if you please"!

797
00:54:47.776 --> 00:54:49.528
Making a few friends. Andy?

798
00:54:50.570 --> 00:54:52.531
I wouldn't say "friends".

799
00:54:52.614 --> 00:54:56.618
I'm a convicted murderer
who provides sound financial planning.

800
00:54:56.701 --> 00:54:59.037
It's a wonderful pet to have.

801
00:54:59.121 --> 00:55:01.039
Got you out of the laundry. though.

802
00:55:01.123 --> 00:55:03.333
Well. it might do more than that.

803
00:55:03.417 --> 00:55:06.420
How about expanding the library?
Get some new books in there.

804
00:55:06.503 --> 00:55:09.215
If you're gonna ask for something.
ask for a pool table.

805
00:55:09.298 --> 00:55:11.759
- Right.
- How do you expect to do that?

806
00:55:11.843 --> 00:55:17.098
I mean. get new books in here.
Mr. Dufresne. if you please?

807
00:55:17.181 --> 00:55:18.933
Ask the Warden for funds.

808
00:55:19.016 --> 00:55:20.268
(LAUGHTER)

809
00:55:20.351 --> 00:55:23.646
Son. son. Six wardens
have been through here in my tenure.

810
00:55:23.729 --> 00:55:27.358
and I've learned one immutable. universal truth.

811
00:55:27.442 --> 00:55:29.152
Not one of them born...

812
00:55:29.152 --> 00:55:34.115
whose asshole wouldn't pucker up tighter than
a snare drum when you asked them for funds.

813
00:55:34.198 --> 00:55:36.492
The budget's stretched thin. as it is.

814
00:55:36.576 --> 00:55:37.827
I see.

815
00:55:37.910 --> 00:55:41.456
Perhaps I could write to the State Senate
and request funds from them.

816
00:55:41.581 --> 00:55:45.961
As far as they're concerned. there's only three
WAYS TO SPEND MONEY WHEN IT COMES TO PRISONS:

817
00:55:46.044 --> 00:55:48.130
more walls. more bars and more guards.

818
00:55:48.213 --> 00:55:52.634
Still. I'd like to try. with your permission.
A letter a week. They can't ignore me forever.

819
00:55:52.718 --> 00:55:54.261
Sure can.

820
00:55:54.344 --> 00:55:57.222
But you write your letters. if it makes you happy.

821
00:55:57.306 --> 00:55:59.600
I'll even mail them for you. How's that?

822
00:56:01.518 --> 00:56:04.563
<i>RED: So. Andy started writing a letter a week.</i>

823
00:56:04.646 --> 00:56:06.732
<i>just like he said.</i>

824
00:56:10.777 --> 00:56:14.907
<i>And. just like Norton said. Andy got no answers.</i>

825
00:56:22.749 --> 00:56:28.254
<i>The following April. Andy did tax returns
for half the guards at Shawshank.</i>

826
00:56:28.338 --> 00:56:31.424
<i>The year after that. he did them all...</i>

827
00:56:31.507 --> 00:56:33.593
<i>including the Warden's.</i>

828
00:56:34.969 --> 00:56:38.765
<i>The year after that. they rescheduled
the start of the intramural season</i>

829
00:56:38.848 --> 00:56:40.934
<i>to coincide with tax season.</i>

830
00:56:43.227 --> 00:56:47.440
<i>The guards on the opposing teams
all remembered to bring their W-2s.</i>

831
00:56:47.523 --> 00:56:51.653
So. Moresby Prison issued you your gun.
but you had to pay for it?

832
00:56:51.736 --> 00:56:53.488
Damn right. The holster. too.

833
00:56:53.571 --> 00:56:54.822
That's tax-deductible.

834
00:56:54.906 --> 00:56:56.074
You can write that off.

835
00:56:56.157 --> 00:56:59.494
<i>RED: Yes. sir.
Andy was a regular cottage industry.</i>

836
00:56:59.577 --> 00:57:02.623
<i>In fact. it got so busy at tax time...</i>

837
00:57:02.706 --> 00:57:04.750
<i>he was allowed a staff.</i>

838
00:57:04.833 --> 00:57:07.294
Hey. Red. can you hand me a stack of 1040s?

839
00:57:07.378 --> 00:57:10.047
<i>It got me out of the wood shop
a month out of the year.</i>

840
00:57:10.130 --> 00:57:12.800
<i>and that was fine by me.</i>

841
00:57:12.883 --> 00:57:16.261
<i>And still...he kept sending those letters.</i>

842
00:57:21.558 --> 00:57:23.394
Red. Andy.

843
00:57:23.477 --> 00:57:24.687
It's Brooks.

844
00:57:24.770 --> 00:57:27.231
(MEN SHOUTING)
- Watch the door.

845
00:57:27.314 --> 00:57:28.899
Please. Brooks.

846
00:57:28.982 --> 00:57:30.984
- Just calm the fuck down.
- Stay back!

847
00:57:31.068 --> 00:57:33.153
- Stay back!
- What the hell's going on?

848
00:57:33.237 --> 00:57:36.323
You tell me. One second he's fine.
Then out comes the knife.

849
00:57:36.407 --> 00:57:38.868
Brooks. we can talk about this. Right?

850
00:57:38.952 --> 00:57:41.079
Nothing to talk about. goddamn it!

851
00:57:41.162 --> 00:57:42.872
I'm gonna cut his fucking throat.

852
00:57:42.956 --> 00:57:44.833
Heywood? Wait. what's he done to you?

853
00:57:44.916 --> 00:57:47.043
It's what they done!

854
00:57:47.127 --> 00:57:48.545
I...I got no choice...

855
00:57:48.628 --> 00:57:51.297
You're not gonna hurt him.
Even Heywood knows that.

856
00:57:51.381 --> 00:57:54.008
- Right. Heywood?
- I...I know that. sure.

857
00:57:54.092 --> 00:57:57.512
You won't hurt him. because he's a friend.
and you're a reasonable man.

858
00:57:57.595 --> 00:57:58.888
That's right. Right. guys?

859
00:57:58.972 --> 00:58:02.350
- Yes.
- So. put the knife down. Brooks. look at me.

860
00:58:02.434 --> 00:58:04.269
Put the knife down.

861
00:58:05.353 --> 00:58:06.521
Brooks...

862
00:58:06.604 --> 00:58:08.857
Look at his neck. for God's sake.

863
00:58:08.940 --> 00:58:11.276
Brooks. look at his neck. It's bleeding.

864
00:58:11.359 --> 00:58:12.527
(HEYWOOD GASPS)

865
00:58:12.610 --> 00:58:14.195
It's the only...

866
00:58:14.279 --> 00:58:16.574
It's the only way they'd let me stay.

867
00:58:16.657 --> 00:58:19.243
Come on. This is crazy.
You don't want to do this.

868
00:58:19.243 --> 00:58:21.328
Put it down.

869
00:58:22.663 --> 00:58:25.040
(BROOKS SOBS)

870
00:58:28.752 --> 00:58:33.466
Come on. Take it easy.
You're going to be all right.

871
00:58:33.549 --> 00:58:34.925
HEYWOOD: Him?

872
00:58:35.009 --> 00:58:38.679
Hell. what about me?
Crazy old fool damn near cut my throat.

873
00:58:38.762 --> 00:58:41.390
RED: Shit. Heywood.
you've had worse from shaving.

874
00:58:41.474 --> 00:58:43.726
What the hell did you do to set him off. anyway?

875
00:58:43.809 --> 00:58:46.145
Nothing. I come in here to say fare-thee-well.

876
00:58:46.228 --> 00:58:49.356
Ain't you heard? His parole's come through.

877
00:58:51.400 --> 00:58:54.529
I just don't understand what happened in there.
That's all.

878
00:58:54.613 --> 00:58:57.199
The old man's as crazy
as a rat in a tin shithouse.

879
00:58:57.282 --> 00:58:59.493
Oh. Heywood. that's enough out of you.

880
00:58:59.576 --> 00:59:02.579
- I heard he had you shitting in your pants.
- Fuck you!

881
00:59:02.662 --> 00:59:04.039
Would you knock it off?

882
00:59:04.122 --> 00:59:06.458
Brooks ain't no bug.

883
00:59:06.541 --> 00:59:08.418
He's just...

884
00:59:10.295 --> 00:59:12.130
He's just institutionalized.

885
00:59:13.465 --> 00:59:15.133
Institutionalized. my ass.

886
00:59:15.217 --> 00:59:19.512
The man's been in here 50 years. Heywood.
50 years.

887
00:59:19.596 --> 00:59:21.306
This is all he knows.

888
00:59:21.389 --> 00:59:23.850
In here. he's an important man.

889
00:59:23.934 --> 00:59:25.393
He's an educated man.

890
00:59:25.477 --> 00:59:27.562
Outside. he's nothing.

891
00:59:29.731 --> 00:59:32.360
Just a used-up con with arthritis in both hands.

892
00:59:32.443 --> 00:59:35.655
Probably couldn't get a library card if he tried.

893
00:59:35.738 --> 00:59:37.823
You know what I'm trying to say?

894
00:59:37.907 --> 00:59:40.660
Red. I do believe you're talking out of your ass.

895
00:59:41.911 --> 00:59:44.830
You believe whatever you want. Floyd.

896
00:59:44.830 --> 00:59:47.375
But I'm telling you. these walls are funny.

897
00:59:48.793 --> 00:59:50.878
First you hate 'em...

898
00:59:52.421 --> 00:59:54.507
..then you get used to 'em.

899
00:59:56.133 --> 00:59:58.761
Enough time passes...

900
00:59:58.844 --> 01:00:01.806
you get so you depend on 'em.

901
01:00:01.889 --> 01:00:04.225
That's institutionalized.

902
01:00:04.308 --> 01:00:05.685
JIGGER: Shit.

903
01:00:05.685 --> 01:00:07.311
You can never get like that.

904
01:00:07.395 --> 01:00:09.314
Oh. yeah?

905
01:00:09.398 --> 01:00:11.984
Say that when you've been here
as long as Brooks has.

906
01:00:12.067 --> 01:00:13.944
Goddamn right.

907
01:00:16.279 --> 01:00:18.824
They send you here for life.

908
01:00:18.949 --> 01:00:21.034
That's exactly what they take.

909
01:00:22.953 --> 01:00:25.038
The part that counts. anyway.

910
01:00:28.083 --> 01:00:31.420
(JAKE SCREECHES)

911
01:00:32.546 --> 01:00:34.715
I can't take care of you no more. Jake.

912
01:00:36.633 --> 01:00:38.468
You go on. now.

913
01:00:39.553 --> 01:00:44.224
You're free.

914
01:01:00.116 --> 01:01:01.993
Bye.

915
01:01:03.077 --> 01:01:04.996
Good luck. Brooks.

916
01:01:41.617 --> 01:01:44.328
<i>BROOKS: Dear fellas...</i>

917
01:01:44.411 --> 01:01:48.624
<i>I can't believe
how fast things move on the outside.</i>

918
01:01:48.707 --> 01:01:49.958
(HORN BLARES)

919
01:01:50.042 --> 01:01:53.086
Watch it. old-timer! Are you trying to get killed?

920
01:01:53.170 --> 01:01:56.507
<i>I saw an automobile once. when I was a kid.</i>

921
01:01:56.590 --> 01:01:59.510
<i>but now...they're everywhere.</i>

922
01:02:03.723 --> 01:02:07.310
<i>The world went and got itself
in a big damn hurry.</i>

923
01:02:23.701 --> 01:02:29.999
<i>The parole board got me into
this halfway house called The Brewer.</i>

924
01:02:30.083 --> 01:02:33.878
<i>and a job bagging groceries at the Foodway.</i>

925
01:02:35.922 --> 01:02:41.262
<i>It's hard work. and I try to keep up.
but my hands hurt most of the time.</i>

926
01:02:41.345 --> 01:02:43.347
WOMAN: Make sure your man double-bags.

927
01:02:43.430 --> 01:02:45.683
Last time. the bottom near came out.

928
01:02:45.766 --> 01:02:49.061
Make sure you double-bag. like the lady says.
Understand?

929
01:02:49.144 --> 01:02:50.604
Yes. sir. I surely will.

930
01:02:50.688 --> 01:02:54.483
<i>BROOKS: I don't think
the store manager likes me very much.</i>

931
01:02:54.566 --> 01:02:56.360
(PIGEONS COOING)

932
01:02:57.444 --> 01:03:02.241
<i>Sometimes. after work.
I go to the park and feed the birds.</i>

933
01:03:02.324 --> 01:03:07.705
<i>I keep thinking Jake might just show up
and say hello.</i>

934
01:03:07.788 --> 01:03:09.581
<i>But he never does.</i>

935
01:03:10.666 --> 01:03:16.046
<i>And I hope. wherever he is.
he's doing OK and making new friends.</i>

936
01:03:19.551 --> 01:03:22.470
<i>I have trouble sleeping at night.</i>

937
01:03:22.554 --> 01:03:25.348
<i>I have bad dreams. like I'm falling.</i>

938
01:03:26.433 --> 01:03:28.351
<i>I wake up. scared.</i>

939
01:03:28.435 --> 01:03:32.439
<i>Sometimes it takes me a while
to remember where I am.</i>

940
01:03:34.065 --> 01:03:35.525
<i>Maybe I should get me a gun</i>

941
01:03:35.608 --> 01:03:39.487
<i>and rob the Foodway. so they'd send me home.</i>

942
01:03:39.571 --> 01:03:41.906
<i>I could shoot the manager. while I was at it.</i>

943
01:03:41.990 --> 01:03:43.950
<i>Sort of like a bonus.</i>

944
01:03:45.452 --> 01:03:49.706
<i>I guess I'm too old for that sort of nonsense
any more.</i>

945
01:03:49.789 --> 01:03:51.833
<i>I don't like it here.</i>

946
01:03:51.916 --> 01:03:54.586
<i>I'm tired of being afraid all the time.</i>

947
01:03:54.669 --> 01:03:55.754
<i>I've decided...</i>

948
01:03:55.837 --> 01:03:57.715
<i>not to stay.</i>

949
01:04:09.101 --> 01:04:12.605
<i>I doubt they'll kick up any fuss.</i>

950
01:04:12.688 --> 01:04:14.774
<i>Not for an old crook like me.</i>

951
01:04:29.622 --> 01:04:31.540
(SCRAPING)

952
01:05:17.838 --> 01:05:21.884
"I doubt they'll kick up any fuss.
Not for an old crook like me.

953
01:05:23.052 --> 01:05:27.098
PS. Tell Heywood
I'm sorry I put a knife to his throat.

954
01:05:27.098 --> 01:05:29.183
No hard feelings. Brooks."

955
01:05:39.902 --> 01:05:41.988
He should have died in here.

956
01:05:47.410 --> 01:05:51.915
HADLEY: What the fuck have you done?
It's a goddamn mess. I'll tell you that.

957
01:05:56.628 --> 01:05:58.046
What's all this?

958
01:05:58.130 --> 01:06:02.009
You tell me. fuck-stick.
They're all addressed to you.

959
01:06:02.092 --> 01:06:03.385
Take it.

960
01:06:12.352 --> 01:06:13.937
"Dear Mr. Dufresne...

961
01:06:15.022 --> 01:06:17.024
In response to your repeated enquiries.

962
01:06:17.107 --> 01:06:21.820
the State has allocated the enclosed funds
for your library project."

963
01:06:21.903 --> 01:06:23.280
This is 200 dollars.

964
01:06:24.323 --> 01:06:28.244
"In addition. the Library District
has generously responded

965
01:06:28.328 --> 01:06:31.039
with a charitable donation
of used books and sundries.

966
01:06:31.122 --> 01:06:33.207
We trust this will fill your needs.

967
01:06:33.291 --> 01:06:37.420
We now consider the matter closed.
Please stop sending us letters."

968
01:06:37.503 --> 01:06:40.340
I want all this cleared out
before the Warden gets back.

969
01:06:40.423 --> 01:06:42.091
Yes. sir.

970
01:06:45.887 --> 01:06:47.263
Good for you. Andy.

971
01:06:49.891 --> 01:06:51.350
Wow!

972
01:06:52.435 --> 01:06:54.520
It only took six years.

973
01:06:55.813 --> 01:06:58.691
From now on.
I'll write two letters a week. instead of one.

974
01:06:58.775 --> 01:07:02.320
Oh. I believe you're crazy enough.
You'd better get all this stuff out.

975
01:07:02.403 --> 01:07:03.571
like the Captain said.

976
01:07:03.654 --> 01:07:07.534
Now. I'm gonna go pinch a loaf.
When I come back. this is all gone. right?

977
01:07:13.707 --> 01:07:15.709
Wow.

978
01:07:45.824 --> 01:07:48.535
<i>♪♪MOZART:
Duettino from The Marriage Of Figaro</i>

979
01:07:49.994 --> 01:07:52.580
<i>♪♪ Sull'aria...</i>

980
01:07:56.209 --> 01:07:57.210
Andy.

981
01:07:57.293 --> 01:07:58.628
do you hear that?

982
01:07:58.711 --> 01:08:02.423
<i>♪♪ ..zeffiretto</i>

983
01:08:10.890 --> 01:08:12.725
<i>(LOCKS DOOR)</i>

984
01:08:14.644 --> 01:08:22.486
<i>♪♪ Questa sera spirera</i>

985
01:08:31.203 --> 01:08:32.538
<i>(FEEDBACK HISSES)</i>

986
01:08:34.790 --> 01:08:37.710
<i>(MUSIC OVER LOUDSPEAKERS)</i>

987
01:08:41.714 --> 01:08:43.799
<i>(ARIA CONTINUES)</i>

988
01:08:52.933 --> 01:08:57.229
<i>♪♪ Sotto i pini</i>

989
01:08:57.313 --> 01:09:02.527
<i>♪♪ Del boschetto</i>

990
01:09:04.029 --> 01:09:06.406
<i>♪♪ Sotto i pini...</i>

991
01:09:06.489 --> 01:09:09.367
(BANGING AT DOOR) Dufresne?

992
01:09:09.451 --> 01:09:11.036
Dufresne?

993
01:09:11.119 --> 01:09:13.204
Andy. let me out.

994
01:09:15.915 --> 01:09:19.461
Andy?

995
01:09:19.544 --> 01:09:24.716
<i>RED: I have no idea to this day
what those two Italian ladies were singing about.</i>

996
01:09:24.799 --> 01:09:27.218
<i>The truth is. I don't want to know.</i>

997
01:09:27.302 --> 01:09:29.387
<i>Some things are best left unsaid.</i>

998
01:09:33.475 --> 01:09:38.522
<i>I like to think they were singing about something
so beautiful. it can't be expressed in words...</i>

999
01:09:38.606 --> 01:09:40.983
<i>and makes your heart ache because of it.</i>

1000
01:09:43.194 --> 01:09:45.905
<i>I tell you. those voices soared...</i>

1001
01:09:45.988 --> 01:09:50.534
<i>higher and farther
than anybody in a grey place dares to dream.</i>

1002
01:09:50.618 --> 01:09:53.996
<i>It was like some beautiful bird
flapped into our drab little cage</i>

1003
01:09:54.080 --> 01:09:57.208
<i>and made those walls dissolve away.</i>

1004
01:09:57.291 --> 01:09:59.627
<i>And for the briefest of moments...</i>

1005
01:09:59.710 --> 01:10:02.797
<i>every last man at Shawshank felt free.</i>

1006
01:10:05.299 --> 01:10:07.802
<i>It pissed the Warden off something awful.</i>

1007
01:10:09.220 --> 01:10:10.346
Open the door.

1008
01:10:13.099 --> 01:10:15.018
Open it up!

1009
01:10:16.228 --> 01:10:18.605
Dufresne. open this door!

1010
01:10:18.688 --> 01:10:20.148
(BANGS DOOR)

1011
01:10:20.232 --> 01:10:21.566
Turn that off!

1012
01:10:21.650 --> 01:10:23.735
(BANGS DOOR)

1013
01:10:25.445 --> 01:10:28.323
(ARIA CONTINUES)

1014
01:10:28.406 --> 01:10:31.159
I am warning you. Dufresne. Turn that off!

1015
01:10:34.663 --> 01:10:36.748
(INCREASES VOLUME)

1016
01:10:45.006 --> 01:10:46.883
Dufresne...

1017
01:10:48.009 --> 01:10:50.095
You're mine now.

1018
01:10:57.645 --> 01:11:00.398
<i>RED: Andy got two weeks in the hole
for that little stunt.</i>

1019
01:11:00.481 --> 01:11:02.900
(HADLEY STOPS RECORD) On your feet!

1020
01:11:04.110 --> 01:11:06.195
- Hey. look who's here.
- Maestro!

1021
01:11:07.697 --> 01:11:11.742
Y-Y-You couldn't play something good. huh?
Hank Williams or something?

1022
01:11:11.826 --> 01:11:14.495
They broke the door down
before I could take requests.

1023
01:11:14.579 --> 01:11:16.372
Was it worth it. two weeks in the hole?

1024
01:11:16.455 --> 01:11:17.707
Easiest time I ever did.

1025
01:11:17.790 --> 01:11:20.835
Bullshit!
There's no such thing as easy time in the hole.

1026
01:11:20.877 --> 01:11:23.504
A week in the hole is like a year.

1027
01:11:23.588 --> 01:11:26.299
I had Mr. Mozart to keep me company.

1028
01:11:26.382 --> 01:11:29.720
So. they let you tote that record player
down there. huh?

1029
01:11:31.847 --> 01:11:33.473
It was in here.

1030
01:11:33.557 --> 01:11:35.225
And in here.

1031
01:11:36.435 --> 01:11:40.689
That's the beauty of music.
They can't get that from you.

1032
01:11:44.610 --> 01:11:47.112
Haven't you ever felt that way about music?

1033
01:11:48.780 --> 01:11:52.868
Well. I played a mean harmonica.
as a younger man.

1034
01:11:52.951 --> 01:11:54.745
Lost interest in it. though.

1035
01:11:54.828 --> 01:11:56.663
Didn't make much sense in here.

1036
01:11:56.747 --> 01:11:59.207
Here's where it makes the most sense.

1037
01:11:59.291 --> 01:12:01.877
You need it. so you don't forget.

1038
01:12:01.960 --> 01:12:03.295
Forget?

1039
01:12:03.378 --> 01:12:05.339
Forget that...

1040
01:12:05.422 --> 01:12:07.508
there are places...

1041
01:12:08.843 --> 01:12:11.387
..in the world that aren't made out of stone...

1042
01:12:11.471 --> 01:12:13.514
that there's a...

1043
01:12:13.598 --> 01:12:15.433
there's something...

1044
01:12:15.516 --> 01:12:18.353
inside that they can't get to...

1045
01:12:18.436 --> 01:12:20.730
that they can't touch.

1046
01:12:20.813 --> 01:12:22.690
It's yours.

1047
01:12:24.108 --> 01:12:25.818
What are you talking about?

1048
01:12:26.903 --> 01:12:28.488
Hope.

1049
01:12:28.571 --> 01:12:30.448
Hope?

1050
01:12:32.283 --> 01:12:34.952
Let me tell you something. my friend.

1051
01:12:35.036 --> 01:12:36.996
Hope is a dangerous thing.

1052
01:12:38.581 --> 01:12:40.625
Hope can drive a man insane.

1053
01:12:41.667 --> 01:12:43.586
It's got no use on the inside.

1054
01:12:43.669 --> 01:12:46.340
You'd better get used to that idea.

1055
01:12:48.759 --> 01:12:50.386
Like Brooks did?

1056
01:13:15.661 --> 01:13:16.703
Sit down.

1057
01:13:21.917 --> 01:13:25.380
It says here that you've served
30 years of a life sentence.

1058
01:13:25.463 --> 01:13:28.091
You feel you've been rehabilitated?

1059
01:13:28.174 --> 01:13:30.260
Oh. yes. sir.

1060
01:13:30.260 --> 01:13:32.345
Without a doubt.

1061
01:13:33.388 --> 01:13:35.723
And I can honestly say I'm a changed man.

1062
01:13:38.309 --> 01:13:40.353
No danger to society here.

1063
01:13:40.436 --> 01:13:42.522
God's honest truth.

1064
01:13:44.858 --> 01:13:46.943
Absolutely rehabilitated.

1065
01:13:56.870 --> 01:13:58.955
30 years.

1066
01:14:00.039 --> 01:14:02.084
Jesus. when they say it like that...

1067
01:14:02.168 --> 01:14:04.253
You wonder where it went.

1068
01:14:07.256 --> 01:14:09.341
I wonder where ten years went.

1069
01:14:14.388 --> 01:14:15.681
Here.

1070
01:14:15.764 --> 01:14:17.933
Little parole rejection present.

1071
01:14:19.768 --> 01:14:21.812
Go ahead and open it.

1072
01:14:21.896 --> 01:14:25.691
I had to go through one of your competitors.
I hope you don't mind.

1073
01:14:25.774 --> 01:14:27.860
I wanted it to be a surprise.

1074
01:14:37.995 --> 01:14:40.081
It's very pretty. Andy.

1075
01:14:41.166 --> 01:14:43.251
Thank you.

1076
01:14:45.003 --> 01:14:47.088
Are you going to play it?

1077
01:14:51.217 --> 01:14:53.303
No.

1078
01:14:55.597 --> 01:14:57.682
Not right now.

1079
01:15:02.854 --> 01:15:04.898
(GUARDS SHOUT)

1080
01:15:04.981 --> 01:15:07.067
Tier 3 South. Clear.

1081
01:15:08.109 --> 01:15:10.153
Tier 4 North. Clear.

1082
01:15:10.236 --> 01:15:12.322
Tier 1 South. Clear.

1083
01:15:15.158 --> 01:15:17.244
Fall in!

1084
01:15:19.955 --> 01:15:22.041
(GATE BUZZER)

1085
01:15:49.694 --> 01:15:51.737
(GUARD'S FOOTSTEPS)

1086
01:15:51.821 --> 01:15:53.406
<i>Lights out!</i>

1087
01:15:53.489 --> 01:15:54.991
(CLICK OF LIGHT SWITCHES)

1088
01:16:00.455 --> 01:16:02.541
(GUARD WALKS AWAY)

1089
01:16:08.713 --> 01:16:10.799
(OUTER DOOR CLOSES)

1090
01:16:19.641 --> 01:16:21.726
(GENTLY PLAYS ONE NOTE)

1091
01:16:27.149 --> 01:16:28.275
(HAMMERING)

1092
01:16:28.358 --> 01:16:30.402
<i>RED: Andy was as good as his word.</i>

1093
01:16:30.485 --> 01:16:32.989
<i>He wrote two letters a week instead of one.</i>

1094
01:16:35.616 --> 01:16:39.745
<i>In 1959. the State Senate
finally clued into the fact</i>

1095
01:16:39.829 --> 01:16:42.707
<i>they couldn't buy him off
with just a $200 check.</i>

1096
01:16:42.790 --> 01:16:49.380
<i>Appropriations Committee voted
an annual payment of $500 just to shut him up.</i>

1097
01:16:49.463 --> 01:16:51.174
<i>And you'd be amazed</i>

1098
01:16:51.257 --> 01:16:52.925
<i>how far Andy could stretch it.</i>

1099
01:16:53.050 --> 01:16:55.928
<i>He made deals with book clubs. charity groups.</i>

1100
01:16:56.012 --> 01:16:58.389
<i>He bought remaindered books by the pound.</i>

1101
01:16:58.472 --> 01:17:00.683
Treasure Island.

1102
01:17:00.766 --> 01:17:02.935
Robert Louis...

1103
01:17:03.019 --> 01:17:04.228
..Stevenson.

1104
01:17:04.312 --> 01:17:05.771
Fiction. adventure.

1105
01:17:07.773 --> 01:17:09.400
What's next?

1106
01:17:09.400 --> 01:17:12.112
I got here Auto Repair and...

1107
01:17:13.155 --> 01:17:14.489
..Soap Carving.

1108
01:17:14.573 --> 01:17:17.951
Trade skills and hobbies. Goes under
Educational. The stack behind you.

1109
01:17:18.035 --> 01:17:20.078
The Count Of Monte Crisco.

1110
01:17:20.162 --> 01:17:22.497
That's Cristo. you dumb shit.

1111
01:17:22.581 --> 01:17:26.376
By Alexandree...Dumass.

1112
01:17:26.460 --> 01:17:31.381
Dumb-ass?

1113
01:17:33.884 --> 01:17:36.220
Dumas. You know what that's about?

1114
01:17:36.303 --> 01:17:37.679
Uh-uh.

1115
01:17:37.763 --> 01:17:40.474
You'll like it. It's about a prison break.

1116
01:17:40.557 --> 01:17:44.561
We ought to file that under Educational. too.
oughtn't we?

1117
01:17:44.645 --> 01:17:48.858
<i>RED: The rest of us did our best to pitch in
when and where we could.</i>

1118
01:17:50.109 --> 01:17:51.945
<i>By the year Kennedy was shot.</i>

1119
01:17:52.028 --> 01:17:56.366
<i>Andy had transformed a storage room
smelling of rat turds and turpentine</i>

1120
01:17:56.366 --> 01:17:59.702
<i>into the best prison library in New England.</i>

1121
01:17:59.786 --> 01:18:03.665
<i>complete with a fine selection of Hank Williams.</i>

1122
01:18:03.748 --> 01:18:07.919
♪♪ Lawd I don't know what I'll do-ooo ♪♪

1123
01:18:08.002 --> 01:18:10.755
♪♪ All I do is sit and sigh... ♪♪

1124
01:18:10.838 --> 01:18:15.593
<i>RED: That was also the year Warden Norton
instituted his famous Inside Out program.</i>

1125
01:18:15.677 --> 01:18:18.388
<i>You may remember reading about it.</i>

1126
01:18:18.471 --> 01:18:21.891
<i>It made all the papers
and got his picture in Look Magazine.</i>

1127
01:18:21.975 --> 01:18:23.643
No free ride.

1128
01:18:23.726 --> 01:18:26.689
But rather a genuine. progressive advance

1129
01:18:26.772 --> 01:18:28.941
in corrections and rehabilitation.

1130
01:18:29.984 --> 01:18:32.319
Our inmates. properly supervised.

1131
01:18:32.403 --> 01:18:35.155
will be put to work outside these walls.

1132
01:18:35.239 --> 01:18:37.324
performing all manner of public service.

1133
01:18:37.408 --> 01:18:41.328
These men can learn
the value of an honest day's labor.

1134
01:18:41.412 --> 01:18:45.124
while providing a valuable service
to the community and...

1135
01:18:45.207 --> 01:18:50.421
at a bare minimum of expense
to Mr. and Mrs. John Q Taxpayer.

1136
01:18:50.504 --> 01:18:53.173
<i>RED: Of course.
Norton failed to mention to the press</i>

1137
01:18:53.257 --> 01:18:56.552
<i>that "bare minimum of expense"
is a fairly loose term.</i>

1138
01:18:56.635 --> 01:18:59.805
<i>There are a hundred different ways
to skim off the top.</i>

1139
01:18:59.888 --> 01:19:02.516
<i>Men. materials. you name it.</i>

1140
01:19:03.560 --> 01:19:06.312
<i>And. oh. my Lord. how the money rolled in.</i>

1141
01:19:06.396 --> 01:19:08.523
If this keeps up. you'll put me out of business.

1142
01:19:08.606 --> 01:19:10.775
- Ned!
- This pool of slave labor you've got.

1143
01:19:10.859 --> 01:19:12.902
you can underbid any contractor in town.

1144
01:19:12.986 --> 01:19:16.948
Ned. we're providing
a valuable community service here.

1145
01:19:17.031 --> 01:19:19.284
Well. that's fine for the papers

1146
01:19:19.367 --> 01:19:20.869
but I've got a family to feed.

1147
01:19:20.952 --> 01:19:22.662
Sam...

1148
01:19:22.745 --> 01:19:25.206
Sam. we go back a long way.

1149
01:19:25.290 --> 01:19:27.625
I need this new highway contract.

1150
01:19:27.709 --> 01:19:29.919
I don't get it. and I go under.

1151
01:19:30.003 --> 01:19:32.046
That's a fact.

1152
01:19:32.130 --> 01:19:34.215
You just have some of this fine pie

1153
01:19:34.299 --> 01:19:36.342
my missus made especially for you.

1154
01:19:36.426 --> 01:19:37.760
and you think about that.

1155
01:19:45.853 --> 01:19:48.772
Ned. I wouldn't worry too much
about this contract.

1156
01:19:48.856 --> 01:19:52.067
It seems to me I already got
my boys committed elsewhere.

1157
01:19:53.944 --> 01:19:56.530
You be sure and thank Maisie for this fine pie.

1158
01:19:58.157 --> 01:20:00.326
<i>RED: And behind every shady deal.</i>

1159
01:20:00.409 --> 01:20:02.620
<i>behind every dollar earned.</i>

1160
01:20:02.703 --> 01:20:05.873
<i>there was Andy. keeping the books.</i>

1161
01:20:06.916 --> 01:20:10.336
Two deposits.
Maine National and New England First.

1162
01:20:10.419 --> 01:20:12.504
Night drops as always. sir.

1163
01:20:42.953 --> 01:20:44.704
Get my stuff down to the laundry.

1164
01:20:44.788 --> 01:20:47.582
- Two suits for dry-clean and a bag of whatnot.
- Yes. sir.

1165
01:20:47.666 --> 01:20:51.419
Tell them if they over-starch my shirts again.
they'll hear about it from me.

1166
01:20:51.503 --> 01:20:53.505
How do I look?

1167
01:20:53.588 --> 01:20:56.299
- Very nice. sir.
- Big charity to-do up Portland way.

1168
01:20:56.383 --> 01:20:58.094
The Governor's going to be there.

1169
01:20:59.512 --> 01:21:01.555
Want the rest of this?

1170
01:21:01.639 --> 01:21:03.724
The woman can't bake worth shit.

1171
01:21:05.101 --> 01:21:06.894
Thank you. sir.

1172
01:21:09.063 --> 01:21:12.817
- He's got his fingers in a lot of pies. I hear.
- What you hear isn't half of it.

1173
01:21:12.900 --> 01:21:15.361
He's got scams you haven't even dreamed of.

1174
01:21:15.444 --> 01:21:17.488
Kickbacks on his kickbacks.

1175
01:21:17.571 --> 01:21:20.449
There's a river of dirty money
running through this place.

1176
01:21:20.533 --> 01:21:23.786
But the problem with having all that money
is you'll have to explain

1177
01:21:23.869 --> 01:21:26.455
- where it came from.
- That's where I come in.

1178
01:21:26.539 --> 01:21:29.041
I channel it. filter it. funnel it.

1179
01:21:29.166 --> 01:21:31.711
Stocks. securities. tax-free municipals.

1180
01:21:31.794 --> 01:21:34.464
I send that money out into the real world.

1181
01:21:34.548 --> 01:21:38.176
- And when it comes back...
- Clean as a virgin's honey pot. huh?

1182
01:21:38.260 --> 01:21:39.469
Cleaner.

1183
01:21:39.553 --> 01:21:43.181
By the time Norton retires.
I'll have made him a millionaire.

1184
01:21:45.934 --> 01:21:50.355
If they ever catch on. though. he's gonna
wind up in here wearing a number himself.

1185
01:21:50.439 --> 01:21:53.692
Now. Red. I thought you had
a little more faith in me than that.

1186
01:21:53.775 --> 01:21:57.070
I know you're good. Andy.
but all that paper leaves a trail.

1187
01:21:57.154 --> 01:22:00.157
Now. anybody gets curious.
the FBI. the IRS. whatever.

1188
01:22:00.240 --> 01:22:03.076
it's gonna lead to somebody.

1189
01:22:03.160 --> 01:22:05.120
Sure it is. But not to me.

1190
01:22:05.203 --> 01:22:07.205
And certainly not to the Warden.

1191
01:22:11.251 --> 01:22:12.545
All right. Who?

1192
01:22:12.628 --> 01:22:14.338
Randall Stevens.

1193
01:22:14.422 --> 01:22:15.590
Who?

1194
01:22:16.674 --> 01:22:21.387
The silent silent partner. He's the guilty one.
Your Honor. The man with the bank accounts.

1195
01:22:21.471 --> 01:22:23.639
That's where the filtering process starts.

1196
01:22:23.723 --> 01:22:26.934
If they trace anything.
it's just going to lead to him.

1197
01:22:27.018 --> 01:22:28.603
But who is he?

1198
01:22:28.686 --> 01:22:30.730
He's a phantom. an apparition.

1199
01:22:30.813 --> 01:22:32.774
Second cousin to Harvey the Rabbit.

1200
01:22:32.857 --> 01:22:35.026
I conjured him...

1201
01:22:35.109 --> 01:22:37.153
out of thin air.

1202
01:22:37.236 --> 01:22:40.072
He doesn't exist. except on paper.

1203
01:22:43.201 --> 01:22:45.578
Andy. you can’t just make a person up.

1204
01:22:45.661 --> 01:22:48.789
Sure you can. if you know how
the system works. where the cracks are.

1205
01:22:48.873 --> 01:22:52.377
It's amazing what you can accomplish by mail.

1206
01:22:52.461 --> 01:22:55.088
Mr. Stevens has a birth certificate.

1207
01:22:55.172 --> 01:22:57.508
a driver's license. social security number.

1208
01:22:57.591 --> 01:22:58.800
You're shitting me?

1209
01:22:58.884 --> 01:23:00.844
If they ever trace any of those accounts.

1210
01:23:00.928 --> 01:23:03.805
they're going to wind up chasing
a figment of my imagination.

1211
01:23:03.889 --> 01:23:05.974
Well. I'll be damned.

1212
01:23:07.267 --> 01:23:09.311
Did I say you were good?

1213
01:23:09.394 --> 01:23:11.563
Shit. you're a Rembrandt!

1214
01:23:11.647 --> 01:23:13.690
You know. the funny thing is.

1215
01:23:13.774 --> 01:23:17.736
on the outside. I was an honest man.
straight as an arrow.

1216
01:23:18.820 --> 01:23:21.156
I had to come to prison to be a crook.

1217
01:23:29.958 --> 01:23:31.334
Ever bother you?

1218
01:23:32.377 --> 01:23:35.797
I don't run the scams. Red.
I just process the profits.

1219
01:23:35.880 --> 01:23:37.924
Fine line maybe but...

1220
01:23:38.007 --> 01:23:40.718
I also built that library

1221
01:23:40.802 --> 01:23:43.429
and used it to help a dozen guys
get a high school diploma.

1222
01:23:43.513 --> 01:23:45.390
Why do you think the Warden lets me do it?

1223
01:23:45.473 --> 01:23:48.226
To keep you happy and doing the laundry.

1224
01:23:48.309 --> 01:23:50.436
Money instead of sheets.

1225
01:23:50.520 --> 01:23:53.231
Well. I work cheap. That's the trade-off.

1226
01:23:53.314 --> 01:23:55.400
(SIREN WAILS)

1227
01:23:58.820 --> 01:24:01.030
<i>♪♪ JOHNNY OTIS: Willy And The Hand Jive ♪♪</i>

1228
01:24:08.831 --> 01:24:10.624
<i>♪♪ I know a cat named... ♪♪</i>

1229
01:24:10.708 --> 01:24:13.377
<i>RED: Tommy Williams
came to Shawshank in 1965</i>

1230
01:24:13.460 --> 01:24:15.504
<i>on a two-year stretch for B&E.</i>

1231
01:24:15.629 --> 01:24:17.756
<i>That's breaking and entering to you.</i>

1232
01:24:17.840 --> 01:24:22.469
<i>The cops caught him sneaking TV sets
out the back door of a JC Penney.</i>

1233
01:24:22.553 --> 01:24:24.305
<i>Young punk.</i>

1234
01:24:24.388 --> 01:24:26.432
<i>Mr. Rock'n'roll.</i>

1235
01:24:26.515 --> 01:24:28.183
<i>Cocky as hell.</i>

1236
01:24:28.267 --> 01:24:30.853
Hey. come on. old boys! Moving like molasses!

1237
01:24:30.936 --> 01:24:32.896
Making me look bad.

1238
01:24:32.896 --> 01:24:34.857
<i>RED: We liked him immediately.</i>

1239
01:24:34.940 --> 01:24:36.984
So I'm backing out the door. right?

1240
01:24:37.067 --> 01:24:38.777
And I got the TV like this.

1241
01:24:38.861 --> 01:24:42.698
It was a big old thing. I couldn't see shit.
Suddenly. I hears this voice.

1242
01:24:42.781 --> 01:24:44.826
"Freeze. kid! Hands in the air."

1243
01:24:44.909 --> 01:24:46.578
Well. I just stand there.

1244
01:24:46.661 --> 01:24:49.456
holding onto that TV. So. finally. the voice says.

1245
01:24:49.539 --> 01:24:51.499
"Do you hear what I said. boy?"

1246
01:24:51.583 --> 01:24:53.960
I say. "Yes. sir. I sure did.

1247
01:24:54.044 --> 01:24:57.672
But if I drop this fucking thing.
you got me on destruction of property. too."

1248
01:24:57.756 --> 01:24:59.883
(LAUGHTER)

1249
01:25:01.760 --> 01:25:04.471
Hey. you've done a stretch in Cashman. right?

1250
01:25:04.554 --> 01:25:08.391
Yeah. Yeah. that was an easy piece of time.
let me tell you.

1251
01:25:08.475 --> 01:25:11.144
Weekend furloughs. work programs.

1252
01:25:11.227 --> 01:25:12.645
Not like here.

1253
01:25:12.729 --> 01:25:15.065
Sounds like you done time
all over New England.

1254
01:25:15.148 --> 01:25:20.236
Yeah. I've been in and out since I was 13. You
name the place. chances are I've been there.

1255
01:25:20.320 --> 01:25:24.325
Perhaps it's time you tried a new profession?

1256
01:25:24.408 --> 01:25:29.497
What I mean is. you don't seem to be a good
thief. Maybe you should try something else.

1257
01:25:29.580 --> 01:25:33.417
Yeah. well. what the hell
do you know about it. Capone?

1258
01:25:33.501 --> 01:25:35.252
What are you in for?

1259
01:25:35.336 --> 01:25:36.962
Me?

1260
01:25:38.464 --> 01:25:40.549
The lawyer fucked me.

1261
01:25:44.261 --> 01:25:47.681
Everybody's innocent in here.
Don't you know that?

1262
01:25:49.517 --> 01:25:52.061
(LAUGHTER BREAKS OUT)

1263
01:25:55.147 --> 01:25:59.319
<i>RED: As it turned out. Tommy had himself
a young wife and a new baby girl.</i>

1264
01:26:00.362 --> 01:26:05.492
<i>Maybe it was the thought of them on the streets
or his child growing up not knowing her daddy.</i>

1265
01:26:05.617 --> 01:26:09.454
<i>Whatever it was.
something lit a fire under that boy's ass.</i>

1266
01:26:13.416 --> 01:26:16.670
I was thinking of maybe
trying for my high school equivalency.

1267
01:26:16.753 --> 01:26:19.339
I hear you helped a couple of fellas with that.

1268
01:26:20.549 --> 01:26:22.759
I don't waste time on losers. Tommy.

1269
01:26:24.344 --> 01:26:26.429
I ain't no goddamn loser.

1270
01:26:28.265 --> 01:26:30.350
- You mean that?
- Yeah.

1271
01:26:32.018 --> 01:26:34.062
You really mean that?

1272
01:26:34.145 --> 01:26:35.814
Yes. sir. I do.

1273
01:26:35.897 --> 01:26:38.025
Good. Because if we do this.

1274
01:26:38.109 --> 01:26:40.861
we do it all the way. 100%. nothing half-assed.

1275
01:26:41.988 --> 01:26:44.073
The thing is. see...

1276
01:26:45.241 --> 01:26:47.076
..I don't read so good.

1277
01:26:48.202 --> 01:26:49.412
Well.

1278
01:26:51.163 --> 01:26:53.207
You don't read...

1279
01:26:53.291 --> 01:26:55.376
so well.

1280
01:26:56.836 --> 01:26:58.504
We'll get to that.

1281
01:26:59.588 --> 01:27:01.340
- R.
- R...

1282
01:27:01.465 --> 01:27:02.842
- S.
- S...

1283
01:27:02.925 --> 01:27:05.094
<i>RED: So Andy took Tommy under his wing.</i>

1284
01:27:05.177 --> 01:27:07.596
<i>He started walking him through his ABCs.</i>

1285
01:27:09.265 --> 01:27:11.851
<i>Tommy took to it pretty well. too.</i>

1286
01:27:11.934 --> 01:27:14.896
<i>The boy found brains he never knew he had.</i>

1287
01:27:17.232 --> 01:27:21.028
<i>Before long. Andy started him
on his course requirements.</i>

1288
01:27:21.111 --> 01:27:23.071
<i>He really liked the kid.</i>

1289
01:27:23.155 --> 01:27:26.325
<i>It gave him a thrill to help a youngster
crawl off the shit heap.</i>

1290
01:27:27.367 --> 01:27:29.411
<i>But that wasn't the only reason.</i>

1291
01:27:29.494 --> 01:27:31.955
<i>Prison time is slow time.</i>

1292
01:27:32.998 --> 01:27:35.250
<i>So you do what you can to keep going.</i>

1293
01:27:35.334 --> 01:27:37.586
<i>Some fellas collect stamps.</i>

1294
01:27:37.586 --> 01:27:40.213
<i>Others build matchstick houses.</i>

1295
01:27:41.256 --> 01:27:43.633
<i>Andy built a library.</i>

1296
01:27:44.676 --> 01:27:46.720
<i>Now he needed a new project.</i>

1297
01:27:46.803 --> 01:27:48.847
<i>Tommy was it.</i>

1298
01:27:48.930 --> 01:27:53.144
<i>It was the same reason he spent years
shaping and polishing those rocks.</i>

1299
01:27:53.227 --> 01:27:56.856
<i>The same reason
he hung his fantasy girlies on the wall.</i>

1300
01:27:58.274 --> 01:27:59.776
<i>In prison.</i>

1301
01:27:59.859 --> 01:28:02.987
<i>a man will do most anything
to keep his mind occupied.</i>

1302
01:28:04.447 --> 01:28:08.910
<i>By 1966. right about the time
Tommy was getting ready to take his exams.</i>

1303
01:28:08.910 --> 01:28:10.953
<i>it was lovely Raquel.</i>

1304
01:28:13.331 --> 01:28:14.957
(CLOCK TICKS)

1305
01:28:28.221 --> 01:28:29.263
Time.

1306
01:28:35.270 --> 01:28:36.563
Well?

1307
01:28:37.648 --> 01:28:39.191
Well. it's for shit.

1308
01:28:39.274 --> 01:28:41.777
I wasted a whole fucking year of my time

1309
01:28:41.860 --> 01:28:45.030
- with this bullshit.
- It's probably not as bad as you think.

1310
01:28:45.113 --> 01:28:48.826
It's worse. I didn't get one thing right.
It might as well have been in Chinese.

1311
01:28:48.909 --> 01:28:51.411
Let's see how the score comes out.

1312
01:28:51.537 --> 01:28:54.164
Well. I'll tell you how the goddamn score
comes out.

1313
01:28:55.958 --> 01:28:57.876
Two points right there.

1314
01:28:57.960 --> 01:28:59.753
There's your goddamn score!

1315
01:28:59.837 --> 01:29:03.674
Goddamn cats crawling up trees.
5x5 is 25.

1316
01:29:04.758 --> 01:29:06.301
Fuck this place!

1317
01:29:06.301 --> 01:29:07.594
Fuck it!

1318
01:29:26.406 --> 01:29:29.158
I feel bad. I let him down.

1319
01:29:29.242 --> 01:29:31.327
Ah. that's crap. kid.

1320
01:29:31.327 --> 01:29:32.870
He's proud of you.

1321
01:29:32.954 --> 01:29:36.082
We've been friends a long time
so I know him as good as anybody.

1322
01:29:36.165 --> 01:29:39.043
- A smart fellow. ain't he?
- As smart as they come.

1323
01:29:39.127 --> 01:29:41.170
He used to be a banker on the outside.

1324
01:29:41.254 --> 01:29:43.298
What's he in here for. anyway?

1325
01:29:43.381 --> 01:29:44.882
Murder.

1326
01:29:46.010 --> 01:29:47.761
The hell you say!

1327
01:29:49.930 --> 01:29:52.224
You wouldn't think it to look at the guy.

1328
01:29:53.267 --> 01:29:55.728
He caught his wife in bed with some golf pro.

1329
01:29:55.811 --> 01:29:57.896
He greased them both.

1330
01:30:05.779 --> 01:30:07.656
What?

1331
01:30:07.740 --> 01:30:10.117
About four years ago.

1332
01:30:10.200 --> 01:30:13.287
I was in Thomaston on a two-to-three stretch.

1333
01:30:14.538 --> 01:30:17.625
I stole a car. It was a dumb-fuck thing to do.

1334
01:30:18.917 --> 01:30:20.961
About six months left to go.

1335
01:30:21.045 --> 01:30:23.088
I get a new cellmate in.

1336
01:30:23.172 --> 01:30:25.050
Elmo Blatch.

1337
01:30:26.092 --> 01:30:27.677
Big. twitchy fucker.

1338
01:30:27.677 --> 01:30:29.971
Kind of roomie you pray you don't get.

1339
01:30:30.055 --> 01:30:32.098
You know what I'm saying?

1340
01:30:32.182 --> 01:30:34.225
Six-to-twelve. armed burglary.

1341
01:30:34.309 --> 01:30:37.520
He said he'd pulled hundreds of jobs.

1342
01:30:37.604 --> 01:30:39.481
Hard to believe. high-strung as he was.

1343
01:30:39.564 --> 01:30:42.609
You'd cut a loud fart.
he'd jump three feet in the air.

1344
01:30:43.735 --> 01:30:45.779
Talked all the time. too.

1345
01:30:45.862 --> 01:30:48.198
That's the other thing. He never shut up.

1346
01:30:48.281 --> 01:30:50.325
Places he'd been in.

1347
01:30:50.408 --> 01:30:53.078
jobs he'd pulled. women he'd fucked.

1348
01:30:53.161 --> 01:30:55.580
Even people he'd killed.

1349
01:30:57.415 --> 01:30:59.793
People who gave him shit.

1350
01:31:00.835 --> 01:31:02.880
That's how he put it.

1351
01:31:02.963 --> 01:31:04.507
So...

1352
01:31:04.590 --> 01:31:06.675
one night. like a joke.

1353
01:31:07.718 --> 01:31:11.013
I say to him. I say.
"Yeah. Elmo. who did you kill?"

1354
01:31:11.097 --> 01:31:12.890
So he says...

1355
01:31:12.973 --> 01:31:16.602
I got me this job one time
bussing tables at a country club.

1356
01:31:17.728 --> 01:31:21.315
So I could case
all these big rich pricks that come in.

1357
01:31:23.734 --> 01:31:25.736
So I pick out this guy.

1358
01:31:26.779 --> 01:31:29.365
go in one night and do his place.

1359
01:31:31.534 --> 01:31:33.536
He wakes up.

1360
01:31:33.619 --> 01:31:35.663
He gives me shit.

1361
01:31:36.705 --> 01:31:38.833
So I killed him.

1362
01:31:39.876 --> 01:31:41.962
Him and this tasty bitch he was with.

1363
01:31:44.256 --> 01:31:46.174
That's the best part.

1364
01:31:47.217 --> 01:31:50.428
She's fucking this prick. see. this golf pro.

1365
01:31:50.512 --> 01:31:52.597
But she's married to some other guy.

1366
01:31:53.640 --> 01:31:55.725
Some hotshot banker.

1367
01:31:57.519 --> 01:31:59.604
And he's the one they pinned it on.

1368
01:32:10.740 --> 01:32:14.578
I have to say
that's the most amazing story I ever heard.

1369
01:32:16.204 --> 01:32:19.083
What amazes me most is
you were taken in by it.

1370
01:32:19.166 --> 01:32:20.793
Sir?

1371
01:32:20.877 --> 01:32:22.545
Well...

1372
01:32:22.628 --> 01:32:26.007
it's obvious this fella Williams
is impressed with you.

1373
01:32:26.090 --> 01:32:28.175
He hears your tale of woe

1374
01:32:28.259 --> 01:32:31.178
and quite naturally wants to cheer you up.

1375
01:32:31.304 --> 01:32:33.347
He's young. not terribly bright.

1376
01:32:33.431 --> 01:32:37.310
Not surprising he wouldn't know
what a state he'd put you in.

1377
01:32:37.393 --> 01:32:39.520
Sir. he's telling the truth.

1378
01:32:39.604 --> 01:32:43.649
Well. let's say. for the moment.
this Blatch does exist.

1379
01:32:43.733 --> 01:32:46.861
You think he'd just fall to his knees and cry.

1380
01:32:46.944 --> 01:32:49.155
"Yes. I did it! I confess!

1381
01:32:49.238 --> 01:32:51.449
And by the way.
add a life term to my sentence"?

1382
01:32:51.532 --> 01:32:54.703
That doesn't matter.
With Tommy's testimony. I can get a new trial.

1383
01:32:54.786 --> 01:32:57.998
That's assuming Blatch is even still there.

1384
01:32:58.081 --> 01:33:00.125
The chances are he'd be released by now.

1385
01:33:00.208 --> 01:33:02.794
They'd have his last address.
names of relatives.

1386
01:33:02.878 --> 01:33:05.047
There's a chance. isn't there?

1387
01:33:07.090 --> 01:33:08.967
How can you be so obtuse?

1388
01:33:09.051 --> 01:33:10.552
What?

1389
01:33:12.054 --> 01:33:13.889
What did you call me?

1390
01:33:13.972 --> 01:33:15.807
Obtuse. Is it deliberate?

1391
01:33:15.891 --> 01:33:17.684
Son. you're forgetting yourself.

1392
01:33:17.768 --> 01:33:20.604
The country club will have his old timecards.

1393
01:33:20.687 --> 01:33:22.814
records. W-2s.

1394
01:33:22.898 --> 01:33:26.902
- with his name on them.
- If you indulge this fantasy. that's your business.

1395
01:33:26.985 --> 01:33:30.989
- Don't make it mine. This meeting is over.
- Sir. if I were to ever get out.

1396
01:33:31.073 --> 01:33:36.079
I would never mention what goes on in here.
I'd be as indictable as you for laundering money.

1397
01:33:37.872 --> 01:33:40.875
Don't ever mention money to me again.
you sorry son of a bitch!

1398
01:33:40.958 --> 01:33:42.835
Not in this office.

1399
01:33:42.835 --> 01:33:44.962
Not anywhere! Get in here now.

1400
01:33:45.046 --> 01:33:48.299
I'm just trying to set your mind at ease.
that's all. Sir. I...

1401
01:33:48.383 --> 01:33:49.759
Solitary. A month.

1402
01:33:49.842 --> 01:33:52.011
- Yes. sir.
- What's the matter with you?

1403
01:33:52.095 --> 01:33:55.348
- Get him out of here.
- This is my chance to get out! Don't you see that?

1404
01:33:55.348 --> 01:33:57.350
It's my life! Don't you understand?

1405
01:33:57.433 --> 01:33:59.894
- Get him out! Get him out!
- This is my life!

1406
01:33:59.977 --> 01:34:01.229
No!

1407
01:34:01.312 --> 01:34:03.147
A month in the hole.

1408
01:34:03.231 --> 01:34:05.817
It's the longest damn stretch I ever heard of.

1409
01:34:05.900 --> 01:34:07.693
It's all my fault.

1410
01:34:07.777 --> 01:34:09.195
Oh. bullshit.

1411
01:34:09.278 --> 01:34:12.574
You didn't pull the trigger
and you certainly didn't convict him.

1412
01:34:12.658 --> 01:34:15.035
Red. are you saying that Andy is innocent?

1413
01:34:15.119 --> 01:34:17.287
I mean. for real innocent?

1414
01:34:17.371 --> 01:34:19.415
It looks that way.

1415
01:34:19.498 --> 01:34:21.542
Sweet Jesus.

1416
01:34:21.625 --> 01:34:23.710
How long's he been here now?

1417
01:34:23.794 --> 01:34:25.838
1947. What is that?

1418
01:34:25.921 --> 01:34:27.464
- 19 years.
TOMMY: 19 years...

1419
01:34:27.548 --> 01:34:30.175
<i>GUARD: Williams. Thomas.
- Yeah. over here.</i>

1420
01:34:32.553 --> 01:34:34.805
- Paxon. Edward.
- Yeah.

1421
01:34:36.014 --> 01:34:38.934
What you got?
Board of Education.

1422
01:34:39.017 --> 01:34:41.687
- The son of a bitch mailed it.
- Looks like he did.

1423
01:34:41.770 --> 01:34:44.815
Are you gonna open it or stand there
with your thumb up your butt?

1424
01:34:44.898 --> 01:34:46.984
The thumb up my butt sounds better.

1425
01:34:48.027 --> 01:34:50.780
Hey. Skeet. come on.
give me that. you shithead.

1426
01:34:51.823 --> 01:34:54.033
- Floyd. come on.
- Over here. over here!

1427
01:34:55.076 --> 01:34:57.162
Hey. Red!

1428
01:34:58.288 --> 01:35:00.707
Come on. will you throw that away. please?

1429
01:35:06.296 --> 01:35:08.381
Well. shit.

1430
01:35:20.643 --> 01:35:23.354
The kid passed. C+ average.

1431
01:35:23.438 --> 01:35:25.523
Thought you'd like to know.

1432
01:35:42.082 --> 01:35:44.168
The Warden wants to talk.

1433
01:35:57.556 --> 01:35:58.682
Out here?

1434
01:35:58.766 --> 01:36:00.851
That's what the man said.

1435
01:36:17.202 --> 01:36:18.995
Warden?

1436
01:36:19.079 --> 01:36:21.164
Tommy.

1437
01:36:26.628 --> 01:36:28.088
Tommy...

1438
01:36:28.171 --> 01:36:32.258
I'm asking you to keep this conversation
just between us.

1439
01:36:33.677 --> 01:36:35.762
I feel awkward enough as it is.

1440
01:36:54.240 --> 01:36:56.325
We got a situation here.

1441
01:36:57.368 --> 01:36:59.412
I think you can appreciate that.

1442
01:36:59.495 --> 01:37:00.955
Yes. sir.

1443
01:37:01.038 --> 01:37:02.540
I sure can.

1444
01:37:02.623 --> 01:37:06.669
I tell you. son. this thing really came along
and knocked my wind out.

1445
01:37:08.421 --> 01:37:10.965
It's got me up nights. that's the truth.

1446
01:37:13.175 --> 01:37:15.261
The right thing to do.

1447
01:37:16.595 --> 01:37:19.599
Sometimes it's hard to know what that is.

1448
01:37:21.309 --> 01:37:23.353
You understand?

1449
01:37:24.729 --> 01:37:26.815
I need your help. son.

1450
01:37:28.233 --> 01:37:30.318
If I'm going to move on this.

1451
01:37:30.318 --> 01:37:33.071
there can't be the least little shred of doubt.

1452
01:37:34.614 --> 01:37:38.034
I have to know
if what you told Dufresne was the truth.

1453
01:37:38.118 --> 01:37:39.703
Yes. sir.

1454
01:37:39.703 --> 01:37:41.329
Absolutely.

1455
01:37:41.413 --> 01:37:44.499
Would you be willing
to swear before a judge and jury.

1456
01:37:44.583 --> 01:37:47.002
having placed your hand on the Good Book

1457
01:37:47.002 --> 01:37:49.713
and taken an oath before Almighty God himself?

1458
01:37:49.796 --> 01:37:51.923
Just give me that chance.

1459
01:37:55.844 --> 01:37:57.513
That's what I thought.

1460
01:38:30.004 --> 01:38:32.089
(KEYS RATTLE)

1461
01:38:44.645 --> 01:38:46.730
I'm sure by now you've heard...

1462
01:38:47.981 --> 01:38:49.358
A terrible thing.

1463
01:38:50.817 --> 01:38:54.404
A man that young. less than a year to go.
trying to escape.

1464
01:38:55.489 --> 01:38:58.116
It broke Captain Hadley's heart to shoot him.

1465
01:38:59.201 --> 01:39:01.244
Truly. it did.

1466
01:39:03.330 --> 01:39:05.415
We just have to put it behind us.

1467
01:39:07.584 --> 01:39:09.002
Move on.

1468
01:39:10.462 --> 01:39:12.339
I'm done.

1469
01:39:13.383 --> 01:39:15.468
Everything stops.

1470
01:39:16.511 --> 01:39:19.347
Get someone else to run your scams.

1471
01:39:20.682 --> 01:39:22.767
Nothing stops.

1472
01:39:23.810 --> 01:39:25.895
Nothing.

1473
01:39:27.647 --> 01:39:29.732
Or you will do the hardest time there is.

1474
01:39:31.609 --> 01:39:34.195
No more protection from the guards.

1475
01:39:34.278 --> 01:39:36.614
I'll pull you out of that one-bunk Hilton

1476
01:39:36.698 --> 01:39:38.866
and cast you down with the Sodomites.

1477
01:39:40.618 --> 01:39:43.121
You'll think you've been fucked by a train.

1478
01:39:44.414 --> 01:39:46.457
And the library?

1479
01:39:46.541 --> 01:39:47.667
Gone.

1480
01:39:47.750 --> 01:39:50.128
Sealed off. brick by brick.

1481
01:39:51.171 --> 01:39:53.966
We'll have us a little book barbecue in the yard.

1482
01:39:54.049 --> 01:39:56.135
They'll see the flames for miles.

1483
01:39:56.218 --> 01:39:58.721
We'll dance around it like wild Injuns.

1484
01:40:00.305 --> 01:40:02.224
You understand me?

1485
01:40:02.307 --> 01:40:04.393
Catching my drift?

1486
01:40:07.479 --> 01:40:09.565
Or am I being obtuse?

1487
01:40:20.701 --> 01:40:22.828
Give him another month to think about it.

1488
01:40:31.337 --> 01:40:33.423
(LOCK CLICKS)

1489
01:41:10.461 --> 01:41:13.506
My wife used to say I'm a hard man to know.

1490
01:41:13.589 --> 01:41:15.674
Like a closed book.

1491
01:41:16.884 --> 01:41:19.637
Complained about it all the time.

1492
01:41:19.720 --> 01:41:21.805
She was beautiful.

1493
01:41:24.016 --> 01:41:26.101
God. I loved her.

1494
01:41:29.104 --> 01:41:31.440
I just didn't know how to show it. that's all.

1495
01:41:33.943 --> 01:41:36.028
I killed her. Red.

1496
01:41:37.488 --> 01:41:39.573
I didn't pull the trigger.

1497
01:41:40.991 --> 01:41:43.077
But I drove her away.

1498
01:41:44.287 --> 01:41:46.873
That's why she died. because of me.

1499
01:41:46.957 --> 01:41:49.042
The way I am.

1500
01:41:57.384 --> 01:41:59.469
That don't make you a murderer.

1501
01:42:02.681 --> 01:42:04.766
A bad husband. maybe.

1502
01:42:08.144 --> 01:42:11.523
Feel bad about it if you want to.
but you didn't pull the trigger.

1503
01:42:11.606 --> 01:42:13.024
No. I didn't.

1504
01:42:13.108 --> 01:42:15.151
Somebody else did.

1505
01:42:16.444 --> 01:42:18.530
And I wound up in here.

1506
01:42:20.907 --> 01:42:22.994
Bad luck. I guess.

1507
01:42:25.913 --> 01:42:27.623
Yeah.

1508
01:42:27.707 --> 01:42:30.001
It floats around.

1509
01:42:30.084 --> 01:42:32.545
It's got to land on somebody.

1510
01:42:32.628 --> 01:42:34.880
It was my turn. that's all.

1511
01:42:35.965 --> 01:42:38.426
I was in the path of the tornado.

1512
01:42:45.057 --> 01:42:48.811
I just didn't expect
the storm would last as long as it has.

1513
01:42:52.898 --> 01:42:54.817
Do you think you'll ever get out of here?

1514
01:42:56.068 --> 01:42:57.737
Me?

1515
01:43:00.031 --> 01:43:01.491
Yeah.

1516
01:43:02.534 --> 01:43:04.494
One day. when I've got a long. white beard

1517
01:43:04.578 --> 01:43:08.081
and two or three marbles rolling around upstairs.
they'll let me out.

1518
01:43:08.498 --> 01:43:10.584
I tell you where I'd go.

1519
01:43:11.793 --> 01:43:13.420
Zihuatanejo.

1520
01:43:13.503 --> 01:43:15.422
Zi...what?

1521
01:43:15.505 --> 01:43:17.549
Zihuatanejo.

1522
01:43:17.632 --> 01:43:19.718
It's in Mexico.

1523
01:43:21.511 --> 01:43:23.722
A little place on the Pacific Ocean.

1524
01:43:24.973 --> 01:43:27.350
You know what the Mexicans say
about the Pacific?

1525
01:43:27.434 --> 01:43:28.894
No.

1526
01:43:28.977 --> 01:43:31.062
They say it has no memory.

1527
01:43:33.523 --> 01:43:36.109
That's where I want to live the rest of my life.

1528
01:43:37.695 --> 01:43:39.781
A warm place with no memory.

1529
01:43:43.075 --> 01:43:45.369
Open up a little hotel.

1530
01:43:47.205 --> 01:43:49.081
right on the beach.

1531
01:43:49.165 --> 01:43:51.209
Buy some worthless old boat.

1532
01:43:51.292 --> 01:43:53.377
fix it up new.

1533
01:43:56.339 --> 01:43:57.548
Take my guests out.

1534
01:43:57.632 --> 01:43:59.717
Charter fishing.

1535
01:44:03.638 --> 01:44:06.265
Zihuatanejo. huh?

1536
01:44:08.893 --> 01:44:12.772
In a place like that. I could use a man
who knows how to get things.

1537
01:44:19.196 --> 01:44:21.907
I don't think I could make it on the outside. Andy.

1538
01:44:28.705 --> 01:44:30.791
I've been in here most of my life.

1539
01:44:32.292 --> 01:44:34.086
I'm an institutional man now.

1540
01:44:34.169 --> 01:44:36.255
Just like Brooks was.

1541
01:44:37.673 --> 01:44:39.925
Well. you underestimate yourself.

1542
01:44:40.008 --> 01:44:42.094
I don't think so.

1543
01:44:44.721 --> 01:44:48.934
I mean...in here. I'm the guy
who can get things for you. sure.

1544
01:44:49.017 --> 01:44:52.939
But outside. all you need is the Yellow Pages.

1545
01:44:53.022 --> 01:44:55.441
Hell. I wouldn't even know where to begin.

1546
01:44:57.527 --> 01:44:59.862
The Pacific Ocean?

1547
01:44:59.946 --> 01:45:01.990
Shit.

1548
01:45:02.073 --> 01:45:05.243
- About scare me to death. something that big.
- Not me.

1549
01:45:05.326 --> 01:45:08.788
I didn't shoot my wife and I didn't shoot her lover.

1550
01:45:10.707 --> 01:45:14.335
Whatever mistakes I've made.
I've paid for them and then some.

1551
01:45:14.419 --> 01:45:16.587
That hotel. that boat.

1552
01:45:18.172 --> 01:45:20.341
I don't think that's too much to ask.

1553
01:45:24.971 --> 01:45:27.890
I don't think you ought to be
doing this to yourself. Andy.

1554
01:45:27.974 --> 01:45:30.018
These are just shitty pipe dreams.

1555
01:45:30.101 --> 01:45:33.063
I mean. Mexico is way the hell down there
and you're in here.

1556
01:45:33.147 --> 01:45:35.190
And that's the way it is.

1557
01:45:35.274 --> 01:45:37.901
Yeah. right. That's the way it is.

1558
01:45:39.653 --> 01:45:41.739
It's down there and I'm in here.

1559
01:45:44.450 --> 01:45:47.244
I guess it comes down to a simple choice. really.

1560
01:45:50.080 --> 01:45:52.124
Get busy living

1561
01:45:52.207 --> 01:45:55.127
or get busy dying.

1562
01:45:58.922 --> 01:46:01.008
Andy.

1563
01:46:03.469 --> 01:46:05.554
Red.

1564
01:46:06.597 --> 01:46:09.017
If you ever get out of here. do me a favor.

1565
01:46:09.100 --> 01:46:10.935
Sure. Andy.

1566
01:46:11.019 --> 01:46:12.353
Anything.

1567
01:46:13.438 --> 01:46:16.900
There's a big hayfield up near Buxton.
You know where Buxton is?

1568
01:46:18.902 --> 01:46:22.739
- Well. just... There's a lot of hayfields up there.
- One in particular.

1569
01:46:22.822 --> 01:46:24.866
It's got a long rock wall

1570
01:46:24.949 --> 01:46:26.868
with a big oak tree at the north end.

1571
01:46:26.951 --> 01:46:29.662
It's like something out of a Robert Frost poem.

1572
01:46:31.039 --> 01:46:33.750
It's where I asked my wife to marry me.

1573
01:46:34.959 --> 01:46:38.755
We went there for a picnic
and made love under that oak.

1574
01:46:40.256 --> 01:46:42.342
I asked and she said yes.

1575
01:46:46.472 --> 01:46:48.516
Promise me. Red.

1576
01:46:48.599 --> 01:46:50.601
if you ever get out.

1577
01:46:50.684 --> 01:46:52.728
find that spot.

1578
01:46:53.771 --> 01:46:59.235
At the base of that wall. you'll find a rock that has
no earthly business in a Maine hayfield.

1579
01:46:59.318 --> 01:47:01.821
A piece of black. volcanic glass.

1580
01:47:04.990 --> 01:47:07.785
There's something buried under it
I want you to have.

1581
01:47:07.868 --> 01:47:09.870
What. Andy?

1582
01:47:09.954 --> 01:47:12.039
What's buried under there?

1583
01:47:13.832 --> 01:47:17.253
You'll have to pry it up to see.

1584
01:47:22.591 --> 01:47:24.678
No. I'm telling you. the guy is...

1585
01:47:25.720 --> 01:47:27.806
He's talking funnier.

1586
01:47:27.889 --> 01:47:31.268
- I'm really worried about him.
- We ought to keep an eye on him.

1587
01:47:31.351 --> 01:47:35.397
That's fine during the day.
but at night he's got that cell all to himself.

1588
01:47:36.481 --> 01:47:37.941
Oh. Lord.

1589
01:47:38.024 --> 01:47:40.068
What?

1590
01:47:41.736 --> 01:47:44.072
Andy come down to the loading dock today.

1591
01:47:44.155 --> 01:47:47.659
- He asked me for a length of rope.
- Rope?

1592
01:47:47.742 --> 01:47:49.578
Six feet long.

1593
01:47:49.661 --> 01:47:51.121
And you gave it to him?

1594
01:47:51.204 --> 01:47:53.873
Sure I did. Why wouldn't I?

1595
01:47:53.873 --> 01:47:55.584
Jesus. Heywood.

1596
01:47:55.667 --> 01:47:57.919
Hey. how the hell was I supposed to know?

1597
01:47:58.003 --> 01:47:59.921
Remember Brooks Hatlen?

1598
01:48:00.005 --> 01:48:01.047
No.

1599
01:48:02.091 --> 01:48:04.302
Andy would never do that.

1600
01:48:04.302 --> 01:48:06.387
Never.

1601
01:48:07.430 --> 01:48:09.515
I don't know.

1602
01:48:11.600 --> 01:48:13.686
Every man has his breaking point.

1603
01:48:16.314 --> 01:48:17.565
Lickety-split.

1604
01:48:17.648 --> 01:48:20.526
- I want to get home.
- Just about finished. sir.

1605
01:48:36.625 --> 01:48:38.711
Three deposits tonight.

1606
01:48:47.095 --> 01:48:49.181
Get my stuff down to the laundry.

1607
01:48:49.181 --> 01:48:52.642
And shine my shoes.
I want 'em looking like mirrors.

1608
01:48:52.726 --> 01:48:54.102
Yes. sir.

1609
01:48:59.399 --> 01:49:01.068
It's good having you back. Andy.

1610
01:49:01.151 --> 01:49:03.904
The place wasn't the same without you.

1611
01:49:06.073 --> 01:49:08.158
(WHISTLES)

1612
01:49:50.993 --> 01:49:53.746
<i>GUARD: Lights out!
(CLICK OF LIGHT SWITCHES)</i>

1613
01:49:58.043 --> 01:50:00.128
(FOOTSTEPS)

1614
01:50:06.051 --> 01:50:08.136
(OUTER DOOR CLOSES)

1615
01:50:24.528 --> 01:50:26.822
<i>RED: I've had some long nights in stir.</i>

1616
01:50:27.865 --> 01:50:30.576
<i>Alone in the dark with nothing but your thoughts.</i>

1617
01:50:30.659 --> 01:50:32.494
<i>time can draw out like a blade.</i>

1618
01:50:32.494 --> 01:50:34.581
(THUNDER RUMBLES)

1619
01:50:38.876 --> 01:50:41.212
<i>That was the longest night of my life.</i>

1620
01:50:51.431 --> 01:50:53.766
(GATE BUZZER)

1621
01:50:57.395 --> 01:50:59.022
<i>GUARD: Give me a count.</i>

1622
01:51:03.359 --> 01:51:05.403
<i>Tier 3 South. Clear.</i>

1623
01:51:05.486 --> 01:51:06.821
<i>Tier 4 North. Clear.</i>

1624
01:51:06.904 --> 01:51:10.491
<i>- Tier 3 North. Clear.
- Man missing on Tier 2.</i>

1625
01:51:10.575 --> 01:51:13.662
- Cell 245.
- Dufresne.

1626
01:51:13.746 --> 01:51:16.665
Get your ass out here. boy.
You're holding up the show.

1627
01:51:19.168 --> 01:51:23.213
Don't make me come down there.
I'll thump your skull for you.

1628
01:51:30.804 --> 01:51:34.183
Damn it. Dufresne. you're putting me behind!
I got a schedule to keep.

1629
01:51:34.266 --> 01:51:37.353
You'd better be sick or dead in there.
I shit you not!

1630
01:51:37.436 --> 01:51:39.271
You hear me?

1631
01:51:45.778 --> 01:51:47.863
Oh. my holy God.

1632
01:52:00.001 --> 01:52:02.087
(SIREN WAILS)

1633
01:52:04.756 --> 01:52:07.467
I want every man on this cell block questioned.

1634
01:52:07.467 --> 01:52:09.677
- Start with that friend of his.
- Who?

1635
01:52:09.761 --> 01:52:10.970
Him!

1636
01:52:12.889 --> 01:52:14.974
Open 237.

1637
01:52:17.977 --> 01:52:20.105
What do you mean. he just wasn't here?

1638
01:52:20.188 --> 01:52:21.731
Don't say that to me. Haig.

1639
01:52:21.815 --> 01:52:24.067
Don't say that to me again.

1640
01:52:24.150 --> 01:52:25.235
But. sir. he wasn't.

1641
01:52:25.318 --> 01:52:27.488
I can see that. Haig!

1642
01:52:27.571 --> 01:52:29.365
You think I'm blind?

1643
01:52:29.365 --> 01:52:32.493
Is that what you're saying? Am I blind. Haig?

1644
01:52:32.576 --> 01:52:33.577
No. sir.

1645
01:52:33.661 --> 01:52:35.704
What about you?

1646
01:52:35.788 --> 01:52:37.623
Are you blind?

1647
01:52:37.706 --> 01:52:40.251
- Tell me what this is.
- Last night's count.

1648
01:52:40.334 --> 01:52:43.629
You see Dufresne's name there?
I sure do. See? Right there.

1649
01:52:43.712 --> 01:52:45.589
Dufresne.

1650
01:52:46.882 --> 01:52:48.551
He was in his cell at lights out.

1651
01:52:48.634 --> 01:52:51.846
It stands to reason
he'd still be here in the morning.

1652
01:52:52.930 --> 01:52:54.807
I want him found.

1653
01:52:54.890 --> 01:52:57.476
Not tomorrow. not after breakfast.

1654
01:52:57.560 --> 01:52:58.602
Now!

1655
01:52:58.602 --> 01:53:00.104
Yes. sir!

1656
01:53:01.230 --> 01:53:03.816
Let's go. let's go!
Move your butts! Move it!

1657
01:53:06.653 --> 01:53:07.696
Stand.

1658
01:53:08.822 --> 01:53:10.073
Well?

1659
01:53:13.451 --> 01:53:14.578
Well. what?

1660
01:53:14.661 --> 01:53:18.123
I see you two all the time.
You're thick as thieves. you are.

1661
01:53:19.165 --> 01:53:20.792
He must have said something.

1662
01:53:20.876 --> 01:53:22.919
No. sir. Warden.

1663
01:53:23.003 --> 01:53:24.462
Not a word.

1664
01:53:26.464 --> 01:53:28.466
Lord. it's a miracle!

1665
01:53:29.509 --> 01:53:31.970
A man up and vanished like a fart in the wind.

1666
01:53:32.053 --> 01:53:33.805
Nothing left but...

1667
01:53:33.889 --> 01:53:36.808
some damn rocks on a windowsill.

1668
01:53:36.892 --> 01:53:38.643
And that cupcake on the wall.

1669
01:53:38.727 --> 01:53:40.353
Let's ask her.

1670
01:53:40.437 --> 01:53:44.442
Maybe she knows. What say there.
Fuzzy Britches? Feel like talking?

1671
01:53:45.526 --> 01:53:46.611
Ah...

1672
01:53:46.611 --> 01:53:48.070
I guess not.

1673
01:53:48.154 --> 01:53:51.032
Why should she be any different?

1674
01:53:51.115 --> 01:53:53.576
This is a conspiracy.

1675
01:53:53.659 --> 01:53:55.870
That's what this is.

1676
01:53:55.953 --> 01:53:57.496
One big...

1677
01:53:57.580 --> 01:54:00.333
damn conspiracy!

1678
01:54:00.416 --> 01:54:03.085
And everyone's in on it!

1679
01:54:03.169 --> 01:54:04.462
Including her!

1680
01:54:05.796 --> 01:54:07.465
(CLATTERING)

1681
01:54:31.239 --> 01:54:32.949
(SIRENS BLARE)

1682
01:54:39.164 --> 01:54:41.041
<i>RED: In 1966.</i>

1683
01:54:41.124 --> 01:54:43.794
<i>Andy Dufresne escaped</i>

1684
01:54:43.877 --> 01:54:45.962
<i>from Shawshank Prison.</i>

1685
01:54:47.631 --> 01:54:50.384
<i>All they found of him
was a muddy set of prison clothes.</i>

1686
01:54:50.467 --> 01:54:52.511
<i>a bar of soap</i>

1687
01:54:52.594 --> 01:54:56.973
<i>and an old rock hammer
damn near worn down to the nub.</i>

1688
01:55:01.354 --> 01:55:06.192
<i>I remember thinking it would take a man
600 years to tunnel through the wall with it.</i>

1689
01:55:06.275 --> 01:55:08.986
<i>Old Andy did it in less than 20.</i>

1690
01:55:27.547 --> 01:55:29.632
<i>Oh. Andy loved geology.</i>

1691
01:55:30.675 --> 01:55:34.220
<i>I imagine it appealed to his meticulous nature.</i>

1692
01:55:34.303 --> 01:55:36.598
<i>An Ice Age here.</i>

1693
01:55:36.682 --> 01:55:39.268
<i>a million years of mountain-building there.</i>

1694
01:55:40.310 --> 01:55:42.729
<i>Geology is the study of pressure and time.</i>

1695
01:55:43.939 --> 01:55:45.983
<i>That's all it takes. really.</i>

1696
01:55:46.066 --> 01:55:48.110
<i>Pressure...</i>

1697
01:55:48.193 --> 01:55:50.070
<i>and time.</i>

1698
01:55:50.154 --> 01:55:53.490
<i>That and a big goddamn poster.</i>

1699
01:55:54.575 --> 01:55:56.618
(COUGHING)

1700
01:55:56.702 --> 01:55:58.078
<i>Like I said.</i>

1701
01:55:58.078 --> 01:56:01.874
<i>in prison. a man will do most anything
to keep his mind occupied.</i>

1702
01:56:04.668 --> 01:56:09.840
<i>It turns out Andy's favorite hobby
was toting his wall out into the exercise yard.</i>

1703
01:56:09.923 --> 01:56:12.009
<i>A handful at a time.</i>

1704
01:56:13.845 --> 01:56:16.014
I guess after Tommy was killed.

1705
01:56:16.097 --> 01:56:18.933
Andy decided he'd been here
just about long enough.

1706
01:56:19.017 --> 01:56:21.227
Lickety-split. I want to get home.

1707
01:56:22.520 --> 01:56:24.606
I'm just about finished. sir.

1708
01:56:46.044 --> 01:56:48.129
Three deposits tonight.

1709
01:56:55.304 --> 01:56:57.348
<i>RED: Andy did like he was told.</i>

1710
01:56:58.390 --> 01:57:01.894
<i>Buffed those shoes to a high mirror shine.</i>

1711
01:57:05.481 --> 01:57:07.524
<i>The guard simply didn't notice.</i>

1712
01:57:07.608 --> 01:57:09.652
<i>Neither did I.</i>

1713
01:57:09.735 --> 01:57:14.073
<i>I mean. seriously. how often
do you really look at a man's shoes?</i>

1714
01:57:48.817 --> 01:57:50.902
(THUNDERCLAP)

1715
01:59:18.241 --> 01:59:24.415
<i>Andy crawled to freedom through 500 yards
of shit-smelling foulness I can't even imagine.</i>

1716
01:59:24.498 --> 01:59:25.666
(GAGS)

1717
01:59:25.750 --> 01:59:27.752
<i>Or maybe I just don't want to.</i>

1718
01:59:27.835 --> 01:59:29.921
(COUGHS AND SPITS)

1719
01:59:32.465 --> 01:59:34.675
<i>500 yards.</i>

1720
01:59:35.718 --> 01:59:38.221
<i>That's the length of five football fields.</i>

1721
01:59:39.263 --> 01:59:41.515
<i>Just shy of half a mile.</i>

1722
02:00:23.100 --> 02:00:24.810
(LAUGHS)

1723
02:00:36.780 --> 02:00:41.327
<i>RED: The next morning. right about the time
Raquel was spilling her little secret.</i>

1724
02:00:41.411 --> 02:00:44.831
<i>a man nobody ever laid eyes on before</i>

1725
02:00:44.914 --> 02:00:47.333
<i>strode into the Maine National Bank.</i>

1726
02:00:47.417 --> 02:00:49.460
<i>Until that moment.</i>

1727
02:00:49.544 --> 02:00:51.421
<i>he didn't exist.</i>

1728
02:00:51.504 --> 02:00:52.839
<i>except on paper.</i>

1729
02:00:52.922 --> 02:00:53.965
<i>WOMEN: May I help you?</i>

1730
02:00:54.048 --> 02:00:56.092
<i>RED: He had all the proper ID.</i>

1731
02:00:56.175 --> 02:00:59.804
<i>driver's license. birth certificate.
social security card.</i>

1732
02:00:59.887 --> 02:01:03.182
<i>And the signature was a spot-on match.</i>

1733
02:01:03.307 --> 02:01:06.352
I must say. I'm sorry to be losing your business.

1734
02:01:06.436 --> 02:01:08.438
I hope you'll enjoy living abroad.

1735
02:01:08.521 --> 02:01:10.314
Thank you.

1736
02:01:10.398 --> 02:01:12.191
I'm sure I will.

1737
02:01:12.275 --> 02:01:14.402
Here's your cashier's check. sir.

1738
02:01:14.485 --> 02:01:16.530
Will there be anything else?

1739
02:01:16.613 --> 02:01:17.614
Please...

1740
02:01:17.698 --> 02:01:20.784
Would you add this to your outgoing mail?

1741
02:01:20.868 --> 02:01:23.078
I'd be happy to.

1742
02:01:23.162 --> 02:01:25.497
- Good day. sir.
- Good day.

1743
02:01:25.581 --> 02:01:30.377
<i>RED: Mr. Stevens visited nearly a dozen banks
in the Portland area that morning.</i>

1744
02:01:31.545 --> 02:01:38.010
<i>All told. he blew town with better than $370.000
of Warden Norton's money.</i>

1745
02:01:38.093 --> 02:01:40.554
<i>Severance pay for 19 years.</i>

1746
02:01:40.637 --> 02:01:42.723
(PHONE RINGS)

1747
02:01:48.687 --> 02:01:50.981
<i>WOMEN: Good morning. Portland Daily Bugle.</i>

1748
02:01:58.656 --> 02:02:00.783
(SIRENS WAIL)

1749
02:02:29.979 --> 02:02:32.024
(SIRENS APPROACHING)

1750
02:02:43.744 --> 02:02:46.747
Byron Hadley?
You have the right to remain silent.

1751
02:02:46.830 --> 02:02:51.460
If you give up the right to remain silent. anything
you say will be held against you in court.

1752
02:02:51.543 --> 02:02:53.420
<i>RED: I wasn't there to see it.</i>

1753
02:02:53.504 --> 02:02:58.425
<i>But I hear Byron Hadley started sobbing
like a little girl when they took him away.</i>

1754
02:03:03.847 --> 02:03:06.642
<i>Norton had no intention of going that quietly.</i>

1755
02:03:22.617 --> 02:03:24.077
<i>Samuel Norton?</i>

1756
02:03:24.160 --> 02:03:27.414
<i>We have a warrant for your arrest. Open up.
(BANGING ON DOOR)</i>

1757
02:03:30.291 --> 02:03:31.418
Norton!

1758
02:03:31.501 --> 02:03:33.169
Open the door.

1759
02:03:33.253 --> 02:03:35.005
<i>I'm not sure which key it is.</i>

1760
02:03:37.882 --> 02:03:39.551
<i>Norton!</i>

1761
02:03:45.015 --> 02:03:47.101
<i>Make it easy on yourself. Norton.</i>

1762
02:03:58.446 --> 02:04:02.033
<i>RED: I like to think
the last thing that went through his head.</i>

1763
02:04:02.116 --> 02:04:03.826
<i>other than that bullet.</i>

1764
02:04:03.909 --> 02:04:07.913
<i>was to wonder how the hell
Andy Dufresne ever got the best of him.</i>

1765
02:04:09.582 --> 02:04:10.666
Carter. James...

1766
02:04:10.750 --> 02:04:14.128
<i>RED: Not long after the Warden
deprived us of his company.</i>

1767
02:04:14.211 --> 02:04:16.464
<i>I got a postcard in the mail.</i>

1768
02:04:18.174 --> 02:04:20.593
<i>It was blank but the postmark said...</i>

1769
02:04:20.676 --> 02:04:23.429
<i>Fort Hancock. Texas.</i>

1770
02:04:23.512 --> 02:04:25.557
<i>Fort Hancock.</i>

1771
02:04:25.640 --> 02:04:27.684
<i>Right on the border.</i>

1772
02:04:27.768 --> 02:04:29.811
<i>That's where Andy crossed.</i>

1773
02:04:29.895 --> 02:04:33.774
<i>When I picture him heading south
in his own car with the top down.</i>

1774
02:04:34.816 --> 02:04:36.902
<i>it always makes me laugh.
(CHUCKLE)</i>

1775
02:04:38.320 --> 02:04:40.363
<i>Andy Dufresne.</i>

1776
02:04:40.447 --> 02:04:42.824
<i>who crawled through a river of shit</i>

1777
02:04:42.908 --> 02:04:44.993
<i>and came out clean on the other side.</i>

1778
02:04:46.244 --> 02:04:48.288
<i>Andy Dufresne.</i>

1779
02:04:48.371 --> 02:04:50.290
<i>headed for the Pacific.</i>

1780
02:04:52.876 --> 02:04:54.920
Hadley's got him by the toes. right?

1781
02:04:55.003 --> 02:04:59.216
And he says. "I believe this boy's
about to have himself an accident."

1782
02:04:59.299 --> 02:05:02.470
<i>RED: Those of us who knew him best
talk about him often.</i>

1783
02:05:02.553 --> 02:05:04.805
<i>I swear. the stuff he pulled...</i>

1784
02:05:04.889 --> 02:05:07.391
"These friends of mine
could use a couple of beers!"

1785
02:05:07.475 --> 02:05:09.560
- And he got it.
- And he got it!

1786
02:05:10.728 --> 02:05:13.105
<i>RED: Sometimes it makes me sad. though.</i>

1787
02:05:13.189 --> 02:05:15.233
<i>Andy being gone.</i>

1788
02:05:15.316 --> 02:05:19.320
<i>I have to remind myself
that some birds aren't meant to be caged.</i>

1789
02:05:20.404 --> 02:05:22.490
<i>Their feathers are just too bright.</i>

1790
02:05:24.033 --> 02:05:26.077
<i>And when they fly away.</i>

1791
02:05:26.160 --> 02:05:30.081
<i>the part of you that knows
it was a sin to lock them up does rejoice.</i>

1792
02:05:31.832 --> 02:05:33.292
<i>But still...</i>

1793
02:05:33.376 --> 02:05:37.547
<i>the place you live in is that much more drab
and empty that they're gone.</i>

1794
02:05:42.135 --> 02:05:44.388
<i>I guess I just miss my friend.</i>

1795
02:06:08.370 --> 02:06:10.247
Please sit down.

1796
02:06:15.836 --> 02:06:17.964
Ellis Boyd Redding.

1797
02:06:18.047 --> 02:06:21.426
Your files say you've served
40 years of a life sentence.

1798
02:06:21.509 --> 02:06:23.886
Do you feel you've been rehabilitated?

1799
02:06:26.014 --> 02:06:28.099
Rehabilitated?

1800
02:06:29.642 --> 02:06:31.728
Well. now. let me see.

1801
02:06:32.770 --> 02:06:35.106
You know. I don't have any idea
what that means.

1802
02:06:36.941 --> 02:06:39.485
Well. it means you're ready to rejoin society...

1803
02:06:39.569 --> 02:06:42.113
I know what you think it means. sonny.

1804
02:06:44.490 --> 02:06:46.576
To me. it's just a made-up word.

1805
02:06:47.618 --> 02:06:49.871
A politician's word so that...

1806
02:06:49.954 --> 02:06:55.460
young fellas like yourself
can wear a suit and a tie and have a job.

1807
02:06:57.880 --> 02:06:59.965
What do you really want to know?

1808
02:07:01.133 --> 02:07:03.052
Am I sorry for what I did?

1809
02:07:03.135 --> 02:07:04.845
Well. are you?

1810
02:07:06.472 --> 02:07:09.058
There's not a day goes by I don't feel regret.

1811
02:07:10.642 --> 02:07:13.771
Not because I'm in here
or because you think I should.

1812
02:07:17.566 --> 02:07:19.651
I look back on the way I was then.

1813
02:07:22.237 --> 02:07:24.281
A young...

1814
02:07:24.364 --> 02:07:27.451
stupid kid who committed that terrible crime.

1815
02:07:31.330 --> 02:07:33.416
I wanna talk to him.

1816
02:07:34.793 --> 02:07:36.961
I wanna try and talk some sense to him.

1817
02:07:38.004 --> 02:07:40.089
tell him the way things are.

1818
02:07:42.258 --> 02:07:44.344
But I can't.

1819
02:07:45.553 --> 02:07:47.639
That kid's long gone.

1820
02:07:48.932 --> 02:07:51.017
This old man is all that's left.

1821
02:07:53.144 --> 02:07:54.646
I gotta live with that.

1822
02:07:55.980 --> 02:07:57.774
Rehabilitated?

1823
02:07:57.857 --> 02:07:59.859
It's just a bullshit word.

1824
02:07:59.943 --> 02:08:05.865
So you go on and stamp your form. sonny.
and stop wasting my time.

1825
02:08:06.950 --> 02:08:08.993
Because to tell you the truth.

1826
02:08:09.077 --> 02:08:11.580
I don't give a shit.

1827
02:08:49.744 --> 02:08:51.830
(GATE CLOSES)

1828
02:09:11.224 --> 02:09:13.310
(SIREN PASSES OUTSIDE)

1829
02:09:37.877 --> 02:09:39.962
Here you go. miss.

1830
02:09:41.964 --> 02:09:43.424
Rest room break. boss?

1831
02:09:49.472 --> 02:09:53.768
You don't need to ask me every time you need
to go take a piss. Just go. Understand?

1832
02:09:54.977 --> 02:09:56.645
Yes. sir.

1833
02:10:06.698 --> 02:10:09.743
<i>RED: 40 years
I've been asking permission to piss.</i>

1834
02:10:10.744 --> 02:10:12.954
<i>I can't squeeze a drop without say-so.</i>

1835
02:10:17.125 --> 02:10:19.211
<i>There's a harsh truth to face.</i>

1836
02:10:21.171 --> 02:10:23.507
<i>No way I'm gonna make it on the outside.</i>

1837
02:10:31.723 --> 02:10:35.185
<i>All I do any more
is think of ways to break my parole...</i>

1838
02:10:36.228 --> 02:10:38.313
<i>..so maybe they'd send me back.</i>

1839
02:10:43.820 --> 02:10:45.905
<i>A terrible thing to live in fear.</i>

1840
02:10:47.281 --> 02:10:50.660
<i>Brooks Hatlen knew it. knew it all too well.</i>

1841
02:10:52.829 --> 02:10:55.623
<i>All I want is to be back
where things make sense.</i>

1842
02:10:56.666 --> 02:10:59.168
<i>where I won't have to be afraid all the time.</i>

1843
02:11:02.046 --> 02:11:04.131
<i>Only one thing stops me.</i>

1844
02:11:05.174 --> 02:11:07.260
<i>A promise I made to Andy.</i>

1845
02:11:28.031 --> 02:11:30.117
Here it is.

1846
02:11:39.918 --> 02:11:42.004
Much obliged. sir.

1847
02:15:05.420 --> 02:15:07.506
(BIRD CALLS)

1848
02:15:20.978 --> 02:15:22.271
<i>ANDY: Dear Red.</i>

1849
02:15:22.355 --> 02:15:24.815
<i>if you're reading this. you've gotten out.</i>

1850
02:15:24.899 --> 02:15:29.153
<i>And if you've come this far.
maybe you're willing to come a little further.</i>

1851
02:15:29.236 --> 02:15:31.822
<i>You remember the name of the town. don't you?</i>

1852
02:15:34.116 --> 02:15:36.202
Zihuatanejo.

1853
02:15:37.244 --> 02:15:38.454
<i>I could use a good man</i>

1854
02:15:38.537 --> 02:15:40.581
<i>to help me get my project on wheels.</i>

1855
02:15:40.665 --> 02:15:42.792
<i>I'll keep an eye out for you</i>

1856
02:15:42.875 --> 02:15:44.920
<i>and the chessboard ready.</i>

1857
02:15:45.962 --> 02:15:47.339
<i>Remember. Red.</i>

1858
02:15:47.422 --> 02:15:49.508
<i>hope is a good thing.</i>

1859
02:15:49.591 --> 02:15:51.635
<i>Maybe the best of things.</i>

1860
02:15:51.718 --> 02:15:53.804
<i>And no good thing ever dies.</i>

1861
02:15:54.846 --> 02:15:57.307
<i>I will be hoping that this letter finds you</i>

1862
02:15:57.391 --> 02:15:59.434
<i>and finds you well.</i>

1863
02:15:59.518 --> 02:16:02.020
<i>Your friend. Andy.</i>

1864
02:16:35.596 --> 02:16:39.475
<i>RED: Get busy living or get busy dying.</i>

1865
02:16:42.019 --> 02:16:44.105
<i>That's goddamn right.</i>

1866
02:16:49.610 --> 02:16:51.737
<i>For the second time in my life.</i>

1867
02:16:51.821 --> 02:16:53.906
<i>I'm guilty of committing a crime.</i>

1868
02:16:55.575 --> 02:16:57.660
<i>Parole violation.</i>

1869
02:16:57.660 --> 02:17:01.373
<i>Of course. I doubt they'll toss up
any roadblocks for that.</i>

1870
02:17:02.624 --> 02:17:04.668
<i>Not for an old crook like me.</i>

1871
02:17:04.751 --> 02:17:06.837
Fort Hancock. Texas. please.

1872
02:17:10.549 --> 02:17:14.678
<i>I find I'm so excited I can barely sit still
or hold a thought in my head.</i>

1873
02:17:15.721 --> 02:17:18.724
<i>I think it's the excitement
only a free man can feel.</i>

1874
02:17:18.807 --> 02:17:21.518
<i>A free man at the start of a long journey</i>

1875
02:17:21.602 --> 02:17:24.521
<i>whose conclusion is uncertain.</i>

1876
02:17:27.399 --> 02:17:29.568
<i>I hope I can make it across the border.</i>

1877
02:17:31.445 --> 02:17:34.239
<i>I hope to see my friend and shake his hand.</i>

1878
02:17:36.617 --> 02:17:39.829
<i>I hope the Pacific is as blue
as it has been in my dreams.</i>

1879
02:17:42.624 --> 02:17:44.500
<i>I hope.</i>
